// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測/IELTS/TOEFL Topic 6
window.I6_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Schools & School Life 學校與校園生活","cards":[{"w":"kindergarten","p":"n.","d":"a school for children aged about three to six","c":"幼兒園","s":"My little brother started kindergarten last September, and now he sings English songs at home every evening.","t":"我弟弟去年九月開始上幼兒園，現在他每天晚上都在家唱英文歌。"},{"w":"preschool","p":"n.","d":"a school for young children before primary school","c":"學前教育機構；幼稚園","s":"Many parents in Taipei send their children to a bilingual preschool because they want them to learn English early.","t":"台北許多家長把孩子送到雙語幼稚園，因為他們希望孩子及早學英文。"},{"w":"elementary","p":"adj.","d":"about the first, simplest stage of school or learning","c":"初級的；小學的","s":"My cousin teaches at an elementary school in Tainan, and she says the children are full of energy every morning.","t":"我表姊在台南一所小學教書，她說孩子們每天早上都精力充沛。"},{"w":"boarding school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school where students live and sleep during the term","c":"寄宿學校","s":"Jason was nervous about moving to a boarding school in the mountains, but he soon made friends in his dormitory.","t":"傑森對於搬到山上的寄宿學校感到緊張，但他很快就在宿舍交到了朋友。"},{"w":"headteacher","p":"n.","d":"the teacher who is in charge of a school","c":"校長","s":"The headteacher gave a short speech at the start of the year, and she asked every student to try something new.","t":"校長在學年開始時做了簡短的演講，她要求每位學生嘗試一件新事物。"},{"w":"classmate","p":"n.","d":"a person in the same class as you at school","c":"同班同學","s":"I forgot my calculator before the maths test, so my classmate kindly lent me hers for the whole lesson.","t":"我在數學考試前忘了帶計算機，所以我的同學好心地把她的借我用了一整節課。"},{"w":"playground","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor area at school where children play","c":"遊樂場；操場","s":"The younger pupils rushed to the playground as soon as the bell rang, and they played until lunch was ready.","t":"鐘聲一響，低年級學生就衝到操場，一直玩到午餐準備好。"},{"w":"cafeteria","p":"n.","d":"a place in a school where students buy and eat food","c":"自助餐廳；學生餐廳","s":"The school cafeteria now offers more vegetables and fruit, but some students still prefer fried chicken and bubble tea.","t":"學校餐廳現在提供更多蔬菜和水果，但有些學生還是比較喜歡炸雞和珍珠奶茶。"},{"w":"locker","p":"n.","d":"a small metal cupboard where students keep their things","c":"置物櫃","s":"I left my heavy dictionary in my locker after class, so my backpack felt much lighter on the way home.","t":"我下課後把厚重的字典留在置物櫃裡，所以回家路上背包輕多了。"},{"w":"dormitory","p":"n.","d":"a large building where students live and sleep","c":"宿舍","s":"The dormitory lights go off at eleven o'clock, so students who want to keep studying have to use small desk lamps.","t":"宿舍的燈十一點就熄了，所以想繼續讀書的學生只能用小檯燈。"},{"w":"semester","p":"n.","d":"one of the two main periods in a school year","c":"學期","s":"This semester I am taking an extra Japanese class, but I still have time to play basketball on Fridays.","t":"這學期我多修了一堂日文課，但我星期五仍然有時間打籃球。"},{"w":"recess","p":"n.","d":"a short break between lessons at school","c":"下課時間","s":"During morning recess the students bought snacks at the school shop, and some of them finished their reading homework.","t":"在早上的下課時間，學生們到福利社買零食，其中有些人寫完了閱讀作業。"},{"w":"attendance","p":"n.","d":"how often someone is present at school or class","c":"出席；出席率","s":"Her attendance was almost perfect this year, because she only missed one day when she had a bad cold.","t":"她今年的出席率幾乎是完美的，因為她只有在重感冒時缺席了一天。"},{"w":"absent","p":"adj.","d":"not at school or work when you should be","c":"缺席的","s":"Three students were absent on Monday because of the flu, so the teacher decided to postpone the speaking test.","t":"星期一有三位學生因為流感而缺席，所以老師決定延後口說測驗。"},{"w":"truancy","p":"n.","d":"staying away from school without permission","c":"逃學；曠課","s":"The school called his parents about his truancy, and they were shocked because he had left home every morning in uniform.","t":"學校打電話給他的父母談他逃學的事，他們很震驚，因為他每天早上都穿著制服出門。"},{"w":"expel","p":"v.","d":"to officially make a student leave a school","c":"開除；退學","s":"The school may expel any student who brings a weapon to class, so the rules are explained clearly on the first day.","t":"學校可能會開除任何帶武器到班上的學生，所以第一天就會清楚說明規定。"},{"w":"detention","p":"n.","d":"a punishment where a student must stay after school","c":"課後留校（處罰）","s":"Ken talked loudly during the test, so he got an hour of detention and missed his football practice.","t":"肯在考試時大聲講話，所以被罰課後留校一小時，錯過了足球練習。"},{"w":"punctual","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or doing something at the right time","c":"準時的","s":"Our English teacher is always punctual, and she expects us to be in our seats before the bell rings.","t":"我們的英文老師總是很準時，她也要求我們在鐘響前坐到座位上。"},{"w":"extracurricular","p":"adj.","d":"done at school but not part of normal lessons","c":"課外的","s":"Universities like applicants who join extracurricular activities, because these activities show teamwork and leadership skills.","t":"大學喜歡參加課外活動的申請者，因為這些活動能展現團隊合作和領導能力。"},{"w":"field trip","p":"n.phr.","d":"a visit made by students to learn outside school","c":"校外教學","s":"Our class went on a field trip to the science museum, and we watched a show about volcanoes and earthquakes.","t":"我們班去科學博物館校外教學，還觀看了一場關於火山和地震的表演。"},{"w":"assembly","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of all the students and teachers in a school","c":"朝會；集會","s":"Every Monday morning the whole school gathers for assembly, and the student council shares important news.","t":"每個星期一早上全校都會集合參加朝會，學生會在會中分享重要消息。"},{"w":"orientation","p":"n.","d":"a time of introduction for new students","c":"新生訓練；入門介紹","s":"New students attended a two-day orientation before classes began, so they knew where the library and labs were.","t":"新生在開學前參加了兩天的新生訓練，所以他們知道圖書館和實驗室在哪裡。"},{"w":"alumni","p":"n.","d":"former students of a school or university","c":"校友（複數）","s":"Several famous alumni came back to give talks on career day, and the students asked them many questions.","t":"幾位知名校友在職涯日回校演講，學生們問了他們很多問題。"},{"w":"homeroom","p":"n.","d":"the class where students meet their main teacher each day","c":"導師班；班級教室","s":"Our homeroom teacher checks attendance every morning, and she also helps us when we have problems with friends.","t":"我們的導師每天早上點名，而且在我們和朋友有問題時也會幫助我們。"},{"w":"bully","p":"v.","d":"to hurt or frighten someone weaker again and again","c":"霸凌；欺負","s":"Some older boys used to bully him online, but he told a teacher and the school stopped it quickly.","t":"有些年紀較大的男孩過去常在網路上霸凌他，但他告訴了老師，學校很快就制止了。"},{"w":"classroom","p":"n.","d":"a room where lessons take place","c":"教室","s":"Our classroom has new air conditioners this year, so it is much easier to concentrate on hot afternoons.","t":"我們的教室今年裝了新冷氣，所以在炎熱的下午專心上課容易多了。"},{"w":"stationery","p":"n.","d":"pens, paper, rulers and other things for writing","c":"文具","s":"Before the new semester, students crowd into stationery shops, and they buy colourful pens, notebooks and sticky notes.","t":"新學期開始前，學生們擠進文具店，買彩色筆、筆記本和便利貼。"},{"w":"staffroom","p":"n.","d":"a room in a school where teachers work and rest","c":"教師辦公室","s":"I took my test paper to the staffroom after lunch, because I wanted to ask my teacher about one question.","t":"午餐後我把考卷拿到教師辦公室，因為我想問老師其中一題。"},{"w":"co-educational","p":"adj.","d":"for both boys and girls together","c":"男女合校的","s":"Most high schools in Taiwan are now co-educational, but some traditional schools still accept only boys or only girls.","t":"台灣大多數高中現在都是男女合校，但有些傳統學校仍然只收男生或只收女生。"},{"w":"single-sex","p":"adj.","d":"only for boys or only for girls","c":"單一性別的","s":"My mother studied at a single-sex school for girls, and she says it helped her feel confident in science classes.","t":"我媽媽以前就讀一所單一性別的女校，她說那幫助她在科學課上更有自信。"},{"w":"state school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school paid for by the government","c":"公立學校","s":"In Britain most children go to a state school, while a small number of families pay for private education.","t":"在英國大部分孩子就讀公立學校，而少數家庭則花錢讓孩子接受私立教育。"},{"w":"janitor","p":"n.","d":"a person who cleans and looks after a school building","c":"校工；工友","s":"The janitor fixed the broken window before school started, so our lesson was not interrupted by the cold wind.","t":"工友在上課前修好了破掉的窗戶，所以我們上課沒有被冷風打擾。"},{"w":"dress code","p":"n.phr.","d":"rules about what clothes people may wear","c":"服裝規定","s":"The school relaxed its dress code last year, so students can now wear sports clothes on hot days.","t":"學校去年放寬了服裝規定，所以學生現在天氣熱時可以穿運動服。"},{"w":"reunion","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people who have not seen each other for a long time","c":"重聚；同學會","s":"My father went to his high school reunion last weekend, and he was surprised that many classmates had become teachers.","t":"我爸爸上週末去參加高中同學會，他很驚訝許多同學都成了老師。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Teaching & Classroom Practice 教學與課堂實務","cards":[{"w":"pedagogy","p":"n.","d":"the methods and practice of teaching","c":"教學法","s":"The new teacher studied modern pedagogy at university, so she uses games and discussions instead of just talking for an hour.","t":"這位新老師在大學研讀過現代教學法，所以她用遊戲和討論，而不是只講課一個小時。"},{"w":"educator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is teaching or education","c":"教育工作者","s":"Many educator in Taiwan are trying new methods, but they still need time and support from their schools.","t":"台灣許多教育工作者正在嘗試新方法，但他們仍然需要學校給予時間和支持。"},{"w":"instructor","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches a practical skill","c":"教練；講師","s":"My swimming instructor is very patient, and she never shouts when I make the same mistake again.","t":"我的游泳教練非常有耐心，即使我再犯同樣的錯誤，她也從不大吼。"},{"w":"lesson plan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a teacher's written plan for one class","c":"教案","s":"Ms Lin writes a detailed lesson plan for every class, but she changes it when the students need more practice.","t":"林老師每堂課都會寫詳細的教案，但當學生需要更多練習時她會調整。"},{"w":"worksheet","p":"n.","d":"a paper with exercises for students to complete","c":"學習單","s":"The teacher handed out a worksheet about the reading passage, and we had ten minutes to answer the questions in pairs.","t":"老師發下一張關於閱讀文章的學習單，我們有十分鐘兩人一組回答問題。"},{"w":"handout","p":"n.","d":"a sheet of information given to students in class","c":"講義","s":"Please keep this handout in your folder, because it has all the grammar rules that will be on the test.","t":"請把這份講義收在你的資料夾裡，因為上面有所有會考的文法規則。"},{"w":"whiteboard","p":"n.","d":"a white board that teachers write on with markers","c":"白板","s":"The teacher drew a timeline on the whiteboard, and the students copied it carefully into their notebooks.","t":"老師在白板上畫了一條時間軸，學生們仔細地把它抄進筆記本。"},{"w":"projector","p":"n.","d":"a machine that shows pictures or slides on a screen","c":"投影機","s":"The projector stopped working in the middle of my presentation, so I had to explain my ideas without any slides.","t":"投影機在我報告到一半時壞了，所以我只好在沒有投影片的情況下解釋我的想法。"},{"w":"group work","p":"n.phr.","d":"tasks that students do together in small teams","c":"小組作業；分組活動","s":"Some students enjoy group work, but others feel that one or two members always do most of the job.","t":"有些學生喜歡分組活動，但也有人覺得總是一兩位組員做了大部分的工作。"},{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a small class where students discuss a subject with a teacher","c":"研討課；專題討論","s":"In the weekly seminar each student shares an article, and the others ask questions about it.","t":"在每週的專題討論課中，每位學生分享一篇文章，其他人則針對它提問。"},{"w":"tutorial","p":"n.","d":"a short lesson for one student or a small group","c":"個別指導課；教學影片","s":"I watched an online tutorial about using spreadsheets, and then I finally finished my science report.","t":"我看了一段關於使用試算表的線上教學影片，然後終於完成了我的科學報告。"},{"w":"role-play","p":"n.","d":"an activity where students act as other people","c":"角色扮演","s":"We did a role-play about ordering food in a restaurant, and it helped shy students speak more English.","t":"我們做了一個在餐廳點餐的角色扮演，它幫助害羞的學生說更多英文。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which someone shows and explains information","c":"簡報；口頭報告","s":"I practised my presentation in front of a mirror many times, so I felt much calmer when I spoke to the class.","t":"我對著鏡子練習口頭報告很多次，所以向全班說話時我覺得冷靜多了。"},{"w":"brainstorm","p":"v.","d":"to share many ideas quickly in a group","c":"腦力激盪","s":"Before writing, the students brainstorm ideas about their dream school, and the teacher wrote every idea on the board.","t":"寫作前，學生們針對理想中的學校腦力激盪，老師把每個想法都寫在黑板上。"},{"w":"hands-on","p":"adj.","d":"learning by doing things yourself","c":"動手做的；實作的","s":"The science class is very hands-on, because we build simple machines instead of only reading about them.","t":"這堂科學課非常注重實作，因為我們親手製作簡單機械，而不只是讀有關它們的內容。"},{"w":"learner-centred","p":"adj.","d":"focusing on what students need and do","c":"以學習者為中心的","s":"In a learner-centred classroom students ask more questions, while the teacher guides them rather than gives long talks.","t":"在以學習者為中心的教室裡，學生提出更多問題，而老師是引導他們，而不是長篇講課。"},{"w":"teacher-centred","p":"adj.","d":"focusing mainly on the teacher talking and controlling","c":"以教師為中心的","s":"Old-fashioned lessons were often teacher-centred, and students simply listened and copied notes for most of the class.","t":"傳統的課堂常常是以教師為中心的，學生大部分時間只是聽講和抄筆記。"},{"w":"classroom management","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ways a teacher keeps a class organised and calm","c":"班級經營","s":"Good classroom management makes lessons run smoothly, and new teachers often learn it from experienced colleagues.","t":"良好的班級經營讓課程進行順利，新老師常從資深同事那裡學習。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"training people to obey rules and control behaviour","c":"紀律；管教","s":"The coach believes in strict discipline, so players who arrive late have to run extra laps.","t":"教練相信嚴格的紀律，所以遲到的球員必須多跑幾圈。"},{"w":"flipped classroom","p":"n.phr.","d":"students watch lessons at home and practise in class","c":"翻轉教室","s":"In a flipped classroom we watch short videos at home, and then we use class time for projects and questions.","t":"在翻轉教室裡，我們在家看短片，然後把上課時間用來做專題和提問。"},{"w":"inquiry-based","p":"adj.","d":"learning by asking questions and finding answers","c":"探究式的","s":"Our school uses inquiry-based learning in science, so students design their own experiments to test ideas.","t":"我們學校在科學課採用探究式學習，所以學生自己設計實驗來驗證想法。"},{"w":"project-based","p":"adj.","d":"learning through long practical projects","c":"專題式的","s":"The project-based course asked us to plan a school garden, and we learned maths, science and teamwork at the same time.","t":"這門專題式課程要我們規劃一座校園花園，而我們同時學到了數學、科學和團隊合作。"},{"w":"rubric","p":"n.","d":"a chart that explains how work will be scored","c":"評分規準","s":"The teacher gave us the rubric before we started writing, so we knew exactly how our stories would be marked.","t":"老師在我們開始寫作前就給了評分規準，所以我們清楚知道故事會如何被評分。"},{"w":"pace","p":"n.","d":"the speed at which something happens","c":"速度；步調","s":"The teacher explained the new grammar at a slow pace, because many students had never seen it before.","t":"老師用緩慢的速度解釋新文法，因為許多學生以前從未見過。"},{"w":"recap","p":"v.","d":"to repeat the main points briefly","c":"扼要重述","s":"At the end of each lesson the teacher asks one student to recap the key ideas, and the others add anything missing.","t":"每堂課結束時，老師會請一位學生扼要重述重點，其他人再補充遺漏的部分。"},{"w":"rapport","p":"n.","d":"a friendly relationship of trust and understanding","c":"融洽關係","s":"Mr Wang has a great rapport with his students, so they feel comfortable asking him about anything.","t":"王老師和學生之間關係非常融洽，所以他們什麼事都敢問他。"},{"w":"visual aid","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture, chart or object that helps people understand","c":"視覺輔助教具","s":"Maps and photos are useful visual aid, because they help students remember new words more easily.","t":"地圖和照片是很有用的視覺輔助教具，因為它們幫助學生更容易記住新單字。"},{"w":"blended learning","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mix of online learning and classroom teaching","c":"混成學習","s":"Since the pandemic many schools use blended learning, and students do some lessons online and some in class.","t":"自從疫情以來，許多學校採用混成學習，學生有些課在線上上，有些在教室上。"},{"w":"student teacher","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is training to become a teacher","c":"實習教師","s":"A student teacher joined our class for six weeks, and she taught us some fun songs about grammar.","t":"一位實習老師來我們班六週，她教了我們一些有趣的文法歌。"},{"w":"teaching assistant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who helps a teacher in class","c":"助教","s":"The teaching assistant helps students who fall behind, while the main teacher works with the rest of the class.","t":"助教協助進度落後的學生，而主要老師則帶領班上其他同學。"},{"w":"drill","p":"n.","d":"practice by repeating the same exercise many times","c":"反覆練習","s":"We did a pronunciation drill for ten minutes, and by the end everyone could say \"th\" correctly.","t":"我們做了十分鐘的發音反覆練習，到最後每個人都能正確發出 th 的音。"},{"w":"dictation","p":"n.","d":"writing down words that someone reads aloud","c":"聽寫","s":"Every Friday we have a spelling dictation, so I review the new words on the bus every Thursday night.","t":"每個星期五我們有拼字聽寫，所以我每週四晚上都在公車上複習新單字。"},{"w":"spoon-feed","p":"v.","d":"to give students answers so they do not think for themselves","c":"填鴨式餵答案；過度灌輸","s":"Some tutors spoon-feed students with model answers, but this does not teach them how to solve new problems.","t":"有些補習老師用範本答案填鴨學生，但這並不能教會他們如何解決新問題。"},{"w":"role model","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose behaviour others want to copy","c":"榜樣；模範","s":"My aunt is my role model, because she became a doctor while helping her family run a small shop.","t":"我阿姨是我的榜樣，因為她一邊幫家裡經營小店一邊成為了醫生。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Learning Skills & Study Habits 學習技巧與讀書習慣","cards":[{"w":"note-taking","p":"n.","d":"writing down the key points while listening or reading","c":"做筆記","s":"Good note-taking helps you remember a lecture, but you should also read your notes again within a day.","t":"良好的做筆記技巧能幫你記住一堂課，但你也應該在一天內重讀筆記。"},{"w":"underline","p":"v.","d":"to draw a line under words to show they are important","c":"在…底下畫線","s":"When I read a hard article, I underline the main ideas, and then I write a short summary in the margin.","t":"讀困難的文章時，我會在主要概念底下畫線，然後在頁邊寫一段簡短摘要。"},{"w":"skim","p":"v.","d":"to read something quickly to get the main idea","c":"略讀","s":"First skim the passage to understand the topic, and then read the questions before you look for details.","t":"先略讀文章以了解主題，然後在找細節之前先讀題目。"},{"w":"scan","p":"v.","d":"to look quickly through a text for a particular piece of information","c":"掃讀；瀏覽搜尋","s":"I scan the timetable for the date of the exam, but I could not find it anywhere on the page.","t":"我快速瀏覽時刻表尋找考試日期，但在整頁上都找不到。"},{"w":"memorise","p":"v.","d":"to learn something so well that you can remember it exactly","c":"背誦；記住","s":"She tried to memorise fifty words in one night, but she forgot most of them by the next morning.","t":"她試著在一個晚上背五十個單字，但到隔天早上就忘了大部分。"},{"w":"review","p":"v.","d":"to study something again in order to remember it","c":"複習","s":"I review my notes for ten minutes every evening, so I do not have to stay up late before tests.","t":"我每天晚上複習筆記十分鐘，所以考試前不必熬夜。"},{"w":"flashcard","p":"n.","d":"a small card with a word on one side and its meaning on the other","c":"單字卡；閃卡","s":"My sister makes a flashcard for every new word, and she tests herself while she waits for the bus.","t":"我妹妹為每個新單字做一張單字卡，並在等公車時自我測驗。"},{"w":"mind map","p":"n.phr.","d":"a diagram that connects ideas around a central topic","c":"心智圖","s":"Before writing my essay I drew a mind map, and it helped me organise my ideas into three clear paragraphs.","t":"寫作文前我畫了一張心智圖，它幫助我把想法整理成三個清楚的段落。"},{"w":"study group","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small group of students who learn together","c":"讀書會","s":"We formed a study group before the final exams, and we met in the library every Saturday afternoon.","t":"我們在期末考前組了一個讀書會，每個星期六下午在圖書館見面。"},{"w":"self-study","p":"n.","d":"learning by yourself without a teacher","c":"自學；自修","s":"The school gives seniors two hours of self-study every afternoon, but some students just chat with friends.","t":"學校每天下午給高三學生兩小時自修時間，但有些學生只是和朋友聊天。"},{"w":"self-directed","p":"adj.","d":"controlled and planned by the learner themselves","c":"自主的；自我導向的","s":"Taiwan's new curriculum encourages self-directed learning, so students choose a topic and plan their own research.","t":"台灣的新課綱鼓勵自主學習，所以學生自己選擇主題並規劃研究。"},{"w":"learning style","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way a person learns best","c":"學習風格","s":"Some people say each child has one learning style, but many researchers believe we all learn in mixed ways.","t":"有些人說每個孩子都有一種學習風格，但許多研究者認為我們都以混合的方式學習。"},{"w":"kinaesthetic","p":"adj.","d":"learning by moving and touching things","c":"動覺的；肢體操作的","s":"My brother is a kinaesthetic learner, so he remembers science better when he builds models with his hands.","t":"我弟弟是動覺型學習者，所以他親手做模型時對科學記得更牢。"},{"w":"time management","p":"n.phr.","d":"the skill of planning and using your time well","c":"時間管理","s":"Good time management is important in senior high school, because students have many tests and club activities.","t":"良好的時間管理在高中很重要，因為學生有許多考試和社團活動。"},{"w":"proofread","p":"v.","d":"to read writing carefully to find and correct mistakes","c":"校對","s":"Always proofread your report before you hand it in, because small spelling mistakes can make a bad impression.","t":"交報告前務必要校對，因為小小的拼字錯誤可能會給人不好的印象。"},{"w":"dictionary","p":"n.","d":"a book or app that explains the meanings of words","c":"字典","s":"I checked the word in an online dictionary, and I also listened to its pronunciation several times.","t":"我在線上字典查了這個字，還聽了好幾次它的發音。"},{"w":"glossary","p":"n.","d":"a list of difficult words with their meanings, often at the end of a book","c":"詞彙表","s":"The biology book has a glossary at the back, so students can quickly look up difficult terms.","t":"這本生物書後面附有詞彙表，所以學生能快速查找困難的術語。"},{"w":"bibliography","p":"n.","d":"a list of books and articles used in a piece of writing","c":"參考書目","s":"Our teacher reminded us to include a bibliography, because we must show where all our information came from.","t":"老師提醒我們要附上參考書目，因為我們必須說明所有資訊的來源。"},{"w":"librarian","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a library","c":"圖書館員","s":"The librarian helped me find three useful books on Taiwanese history, and she showed me how to use the online catalogue.","t":"圖書館員幫我找到三本有關台灣歷史的實用書籍，還教我如何使用線上目錄。"},{"w":"reading list","p":"n.phr.","d":"a list of books students are told to read","c":"書單；閱讀清單","s":"The summer reading list includes five English novels, but students only need to write a report on one of them.","t":"暑假書單包含五本英文小說，但學生只需要針對其中一本寫報告。"},{"w":"grasp","p":"v.","d":"to understand something, especially something difficult","c":"理解；領會","s":"At first I could not grasp how the past perfect works, but my teacher's timeline made it clear.","t":"一開始我無法理解過去完成式怎麼用，但老師畫的時間軸讓它變清楚了。"},{"w":"master","p":"v.","d":"to learn something completely and become very good at it","c":"精通；掌握","s":"It takes years to master a musical instrument, so you should not give up after only a few lessons.","t":"要精通一種樂器需要好幾年，所以不應該只上幾堂課就放棄。"},{"w":"familiarise","p":"v.","d":"to learn about something so that you know it well","c":"使熟悉","s":"New students should familiarise themselves with the school rules, because teachers will not accept excuses later.","t":"新生應該熟悉校規，因為之後老師不會接受任何藉口。"},{"w":"practise","p":"v.","d":"to do something again and again to improve","c":"練習","s":"I practise speaking English with a language partner online, and my confidence has grown a lot this year.","t":"我在線上和語言夥伴練習說英文，今年我的自信心增加了很多。"},{"w":"metacognition","p":"n.","d":"thinking about how you think and learn","c":"後設認知","s":"Teachers want to develop students' metacognition, so they ask them to explain how they solved each problem.","t":"老師們想培養學生的後設認知，所以會請他們說明自己如何解出每個問題。"},{"w":"studious","p":"adj.","d":"spending a lot of time studying and reading","c":"好學的；用功的","s":"Ben is very studious and often reads in the library, but he also enjoys playing basketball with friends.","t":"班非常用功，常在圖書館讀書，但他也喜歡和朋友打籃球。"},{"w":"bookworm","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves reading books","c":"書蟲","s":"My best friend is a real bookworm, and she finished the whole Harry Potter series in two weeks.","t":"我最好的朋友是個十足的書蟲，她兩週就讀完了整套哈利波特。"},{"w":"learning curve","p":"n.phr.","d":"how quickly someone learns something new","c":"學習曲線","s":"Coding has a steep learning curve at first, but it becomes much easier after a few weeks of practice.","t":"寫程式一開始的學習曲線很陡峭，但練習幾週之後就容易多了。"},{"w":"plateau","p":"n.","d":"a period when progress stops for a while","c":"停滯期；高原期","s":"Many language learners reach a plateau after a year, so they need new challenges to keep improving.","t":"許多語言學習者在一年後會進入停滯期，所以他們需要新挑戰才能持續進步。"},{"w":"annotate","p":"v.","d":"to add short notes to a text to explain or comment","c":"加註解","s":"We annotate the poem with our own comments, and then we compared our ideas in small groups.","t":"我們在詩上加了自己的註解，然後在小組中比較彼此的想法。"},{"w":"highlighter","p":"n.","d":"a bright pen used to mark important words","c":"螢光筆","s":"He used a yellow highlighter on almost every line, so the colour no longer showed what was really important.","t":"他幾乎每一行都用黃色螢光筆畫，所以顏色已經無法顯示真正重要的內容。"},{"w":"audiobook","p":"n.","d":"a recording of someone reading a book aloud","c":"有聲書","s":"I listen to an English audiobook on my way to school, and it has improved my listening skills.","t":"我上學途中聽英文有聲書，它提升了我的聽力。"},{"w":"self-taught","p":"adj.","d":"having learned a skill by yourself, without lessons","c":"自學的","s":"The self-taught guitarist never took a single lesson, but he learned hundreds of songs from online videos.","t":"這位自學的吉他手從沒上過一堂課，但他從網路影片學會了好幾百首歌。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Exams & Grading 考試與評分","cards":[{"w":"exam","p":"n.","d":"a formal test of knowledge or skill","c":"考試","s":"The final exam is next Tuesday, so the library will stay open until ten o'clock every night this week.","t":"期末考試在下週二，所以這週圖書館每晚都會開到十點。"},{"w":"examiner","p":"n.","d":"a person who sets or marks an exam, or tests speaking","c":"主考官；閱卷人","s":"The IELTS examiner asked me about my hometown, and I tried to give long answers with examples.","t":"雅思主考官問我關於家鄉的問題，我試著用例子給出較長的回答。"},{"w":"invigilator","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches students during an exam","c":"監考人員","s":"The invigilator walked slowly around the hall, and she collected all the phones before the test began.","t":"監考人員在考場裡慢慢走動，並在考試開始前收走所有手機。"},{"w":"candidate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is taking an exam","c":"考生；應試者","s":"Each candidate must bring an ID card to the test centre, or they will not be allowed to enter the room.","t":"每位考生都必須攜帶身分證到考場，否則將不被允許進入考場。"},{"w":"mock exam","p":"n.phr.","d":"a practice exam taken before the real one","c":"模擬考","s":"My score on the mock exam was disappointing, but it showed me exactly which topics I needed to review.","t":"我模擬考的成績令人失望，但它讓我清楚知道需要複習哪些主題。"},{"w":"past paper","p":"n.phr.","d":"an exam from a previous year used for practice","c":"考古題","s":"Our teacher gave us a past paper from 2023, and we did it under real time limits in class.","t":"老師給了我們一份2023年的考古題，我們在課堂上依照真實的時間限制作答。"},{"w":"multiple-choice","p":"adj.","d":"giving several possible answers to choose from","c":"選擇題的","s":"The first part of the test has forty multiple-choice questions, while the second part asks students to write short answers.","t":"測驗第一部分有四十題選擇題，而第二部分要學生寫簡答。"},{"w":"open-book","p":"adj.","d":"allowing students to use books during the exam","c":"開書考的","s":"The history test was open-book, but it was still difficult because the questions asked for our own opinions.","t":"這次歷史考試是開書考，但仍然很難，因為題目要求我們提出自己的看法。"},{"w":"oral","p":"adj.","d":"spoken rather than written","c":"口語的；口試的","s":"I was nervous before the oral exam, but the teacher smiled and asked easy questions at first.","t":"口試前我很緊張，但老師面帶微笑，一開始問的是簡單的問題。"},{"w":"transcript","p":"n.","d":"an official record of a student's courses and results","c":"成績單","s":"Universities abroad asked for my high school transcript, so I requested an English copy from the school office.","t":"國外大學要求我提供高中成績單，所以我向學校辦公室申請了英文版。"},{"w":"report card","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school report showing a student's results","c":"成績通知單","s":"When I brought my report card home, my parents were happy because my science result had improved a lot.","t":"我把成績單帶回家時，爸媽很開心，因為我的自然成績進步了很多。"},{"w":"mark","p":"v.","d":"to check and give a score to students' work","c":"批改；評分","s":"The teacher stayed up late to mark our tests, so we got them back the very next morning.","t":"老師熬夜批改我們的考卷，所以我們隔天早上就拿回來了。"},{"w":"retake","p":"v.","d":"to take an exam again after failing or to get a better score","c":"重考","s":"He decided to retake the driving test next month, because he had made a small mistake when parking.","t":"他決定下個月重考駕照，因為他在停車時犯了一個小錯。"},{"w":"standardised","p":"adj.","d":"the same for everyone, so results can be compared","c":"標準化的","s":"The GSAT is a standardised test, so students across Taiwan answer the same questions on the same day.","t":"學測是標準化測驗，所以全台學生在同一天回答同樣的題目。"},{"w":"entrance exam","p":"n.phr.","d":"an exam you must pass to join a school or university","c":"入學考試","s":"She studied for months for the entrance exam, and she was accepted by the medical school she wanted.","t":"她為入學考試準備了好幾個月，最後被她想要的醫學系錄取。"},{"w":"scholarship","p":"n.","d":"money given to a student to help pay for education","c":"獎學金","s":"He won a full scholarship to study in Canada, so his parents did not have to worry about the fees.","t":"他獲得了全額獎學金到加拿大念書，所以他父母不必擔心學費。"},{"w":"distinction","p":"n.","d":"the highest level of result in an exam","c":"優等；優異成績","s":"She passed her piano exam with distinction, and her teacher invited her to play at the school concert.","t":"她以優異成績通過鋼琴檢定，老師邀請她在學校音樂會上演奏。"},{"w":"credit","p":"n.","d":"a unit that shows a student has completed part of a course","c":"學分","s":"Each elective course is worth two credit, and students need a certain number of them to graduate.","t":"每門選修課值兩個學分，學生需要修滿一定數量才能畢業。"},{"w":"ranking","p":"n.","d":"a position in a list showing who is better or worse","c":"排名","s":"The school no longer posts each student's ranking on the wall, because it made many teenagers feel stressed.","t":"學校不再把每位學生的排名貼在牆上，因為那讓許多青少年感到壓力。"},{"w":"percentile","p":"n.","d":"a position showing what percentage of people scored lower","c":"百分位數","s":"His score put him in the 90th percentile, which means he did better than ninety percent of test takers.","t":"他的分數落在第90百分位數，這表示他考得比百分之九十的考生好。"},{"w":"high-stakes","p":"adj.","d":"having very important results or effects","c":"高利害的；攸關重大的","s":"University entrance tests are high-stakes exams, so many students feel huge pressure in their final year.","t":"大學入學考試是攸關重大的考試，所以許多學生在最後一年感到巨大壓力。"},{"w":"formative","p":"adj.","d":"used during learning to help students improve","c":"形成性的","s":"Short formative tests help teachers see what students do not understand, and they do not count towards the final score.","t":"簡短的形成性測驗幫助老師看出學生不懂的地方，而且不計入總成績。"},{"w":"summative","p":"adj.","d":"used at the end to judge what students have learned","c":"總結性的","s":"The final exam is a summative test, so it shows how much students have learned during the whole semester.","t":"期末考是總結性測驗，所以它顯示學生整學期學到了多少。"},{"w":"answer sheet","p":"n.phr.","d":"the paper on which students write or mark their answers","c":"答案卡；答案紙","s":"Use a 2B pencil on the answer sheet, and make sure you fill in each circle completely.","t":"在答案卡上要用2B鉛筆，並確保每個圓圈都完整塗滿。"},{"w":"extension","p":"n.","d":"extra time given to finish a piece of work","c":"延期；延長期限","s":"I was ill for a week, so the teacher gave me an extension and I handed in my project on Friday.","t":"我病了一週，所以老師讓我延期，我在星期五交了專題。"},{"w":"crib sheet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small hidden paper with answers used to cheat","c":"小抄","s":"The student hid a crib sheet in his pencil case, but the invigilator found it within five minutes.","t":"那位學生把小抄藏在鉛筆盒裡，但監考人員五分鐘內就發現了。"},{"w":"pass rate","p":"n.phr.","d":"the percentage of people who pass an exam","c":"及格率；通過率","s":"The pass rate for the driving test is quite low, so most people take extra lessons before trying it.","t":"駕照考試的通過率相當低，所以大部分人在應考前會多上幾堂課。"},{"w":"marking scheme","p":"n.phr.","d":"the official guide for scoring an exam","c":"評分標準","s":"Teachers follow the same marking scheme, so students at different schools are scored in a fair way.","t":"老師們遵循同一套評分標準，所以不同學校的學生都能被公平評分。"},{"w":"diploma","p":"n.","d":"a document showing you have completed a course","c":"文憑；畢業證書","s":"She proudly held her diploma on stage, and her grandparents took dozens of photos from the audience.","t":"她在台上驕傲地拿著畢業證書，她的祖父母在觀眾席拍了好幾十張照片。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an official record that you have passed exams or training","c":"資格；學歷證照","s":"You need a teaching qualification to work in a public school, but private cram schools are not always so strict.","t":"在公立學校任教需要教師資格，但私人補習班不一定那麼嚴格。"},{"w":"band score","p":"n.phr.","d":"a level from 1 to 9 given in the IELTS test","c":"（雅思）級分","s":"She needs a band score of 6.5 for her university application, so she is practising writing every day.","t":"她的大學申請需要6.5的級分，所以她每天都在練習寫作。"},{"w":"underachieve","p":"v.","d":"to do less well than your ability suggests","c":"表現低於應有水準","s":"Bright students sometimes underachieve when they feel bored, so teachers try to give them more challenging tasks.","t":"聰明的學生有時在感到無聊時會表現不如預期，所以老師會試著給他們更有挑戰性的任務。"},{"w":"high achiever","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is very successful, especially at school","c":"成就卓越者；資優生","s":"Lucy is a high achiever in every subject, but she still asks for help when she does not understand something.","t":"露西每一科都是成績頂尖的學生，但遇到不懂的地方她仍然會請求協助。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Higher Education & University Life 高等教育與大學生活","cards":[{"w":"undergraduate","p":"n.","d":"a university student studying for a first degree","c":"大學部學生","s":"As an undergraduate she lived in a shared flat, and she worked part-time in a café to pay her rent.","t":"身為大學部學生，她住在合租公寓，並在咖啡店打工支付房租。"},{"w":"postgraduate","p":"adj.","d":"relating to study after a first degree","c":"研究所的","s":"He started a postgraduate course in engineering, because he wanted to design safer bridges in the future.","t":"他開始攻讀工程研究所課程，因為他未來想設計更安全的橋梁。"},{"w":"freshman","p":"n.","d":"a student in the first year of high school or university","c":"新鮮人；一年級新生","s":"As a freshman I got lost on campus several times, but older students always helped me find my classroom.","t":"身為新生，我在校園裡迷路了好幾次，但學長姊總會幫我找到教室。"},{"w":"bachelor's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a first university degree, usually after four years","c":"學士學位","s":"My sister earned her bachelor's degree in nursing, and now she works at a hospital in Kaohsiung.","t":"我姊姊取得了護理學士學位，現在在高雄的一家醫院工作。"},{"w":"master's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a university degree after a bachelor's degree","c":"碩士學位","s":"Many engineers in Taiwan study for a master's degree, because it often leads to a higher salary.","t":"台灣許多工程師攻讀碩士學位，因為這往往能帶來較高的薪水。"},{"w":"doctorate","p":"n.","d":"the highest university degree, also called a PhD","c":"博士學位","s":"Dr Chen completed her doctorate in marine biology, and she now teaches at a university in Keelung.","t":"陳博士完成了海洋生物學的博士學位，現在在基隆的一所大學任教。"},{"w":"dissertation","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of writing done for a university degree","c":"學位論文","s":"He spent his final year writing a dissertation on online learning, and his professor praised his careful research.","t":"他大四整年都在寫一篇關於線上學習的學位論文，教授稱讚他研究嚴謹。"},{"w":"major","p":"n.","d":"the main subject a university student studies","c":"主修","s":"My major is economics, but I am also taking classes in Japanese because I want to work in Tokyo.","t":"我的主修是經濟學，但我也在修日文課，因為我想在東京工作。"},{"w":"minor","p":"n.","d":"a second subject studied at university, with fewer courses","c":"輔修","s":"She chose psychology as her minor, and the extra classes helped her understand her future customers.","t":"她選擇心理學作為輔修，這些額外課程幫助她了解未來的顧客。"},{"w":"faculty","p":"n.","d":"a group of university departments, or all the teaching staff","c":"學院；全體教職員","s":"The faculty of medicine has a new building, and students can now practise in modern training rooms.","t":"醫學院有一棟新大樓，學生現在可以在現代化的訓練教室練習。"},{"w":"campus","p":"n.","d":"the land and buildings of a university or school","c":"校園","s":"The campus is so large that many students ride bicycles between classes, and some even use electric scooters.","t":"校園大到許多學生在上課之間騎腳踏車往返，有些人甚至騎電動滑板車。"},{"w":"professor","p":"n.","d":"a senior teacher at a university","c":"教授","s":"Our professor explained the theory with real examples, so even students without a science background understood.","t":"我們的教授用真實例子解釋理論，所以即使沒有理科背景的學生也聽得懂。"},{"w":"dean","p":"n.","d":"a person in charge of a faculty or of students at a university","c":"院長；系主任","s":"The dean of students met the club leaders, and she agreed to give them more money for events.","t":"學務長和社團幹部會面，並同意撥給他們更多活動經費。"},{"w":"admission","p":"n.","d":"permission to join a school or university","c":"入學許可；錄取","s":"Her admission to National Taiwan University surprised no one, because she had worked hard for years.","t":"她被台大錄取一點也不令人意外，因為她多年來一直很努力。"},{"w":"student loan","p":"n.phr.","d":"money borrowed to pay for university, paid back later","c":"學生貸款","s":"He took out a student loan to pay his fees, so he plans to work for a few years before travelling.","t":"他申請了學生貸款來支付學費，所以他打算先工作幾年再去旅行。"},{"w":"gap year","p":"n.phr.","d":"a year off between school and university","c":"空檔年","s":"After high school she took a gap year to volunteer in Thailand, and it helped her decide what to study.","t":"高中畢業後她休了一個空檔年去泰國當志工，這幫助她決定要念什麼。"},{"w":"exchange student","p":"n.phr.","d":"a student who studies in another country for a short time","c":"交換學生","s":"An exchange student from Germany joined our class, and we taught her how to use chopsticks.","t":"一位來自德國的交換學生加入我們班，而我們教她怎麼用筷子。"},{"w":"study abroad","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to another country to study","c":"出國留學","s":"Many young Taiwanese hope to study abroad, but the costs of living overseas can be very high.","t":"許多台灣年輕人希望出國留學，但在國外生活的費用可能非常高。"},{"w":"internship","p":"n.","d":"a short period of work to gain experience","c":"實習","s":"She did a summer internship at a design company, and they offered her a job after she graduated.","t":"她暑假在一家設計公司實習，而公司在她畢業後提供了她一份工作。"},{"w":"vocational","p":"adj.","d":"teaching skills for a particular job","c":"職業的；技職的","s":"He chose a vocational high school to learn car repair, and he opened his own garage at twenty-five.","t":"他選擇讀技職高中學汽車維修，並在二十五歲時開了自己的修車廠。"},{"w":"apprenticeship","p":"n.","d":"a period of training for a skilled job with an expert","c":"學徒期；學徒制","s":"He spent three years in an apprenticeship with a famous baker, and now he runs a popular bakery in Taichung.","t":"他跟著一位知名麵包師傅當了三年學徒，現在在台中經營一家受歡迎的麵包店。"},{"w":"accredited","p":"adj.","d":"officially approved as meeting standards","c":"經認證的","s":"Make sure the online college is accredited, or employers may not accept the degree you earn there.","t":"務必確認那所線上學院是經過認證的，否則雇主可能不承認你在那裡取得的學位。"},{"w":"elective","p":"n.","d":"a course that students can choose to take","c":"選修課","s":"I took photography as an elective this year, and now I take pictures of the school garden every week.","t":"我今年選了攝影作為選修課，現在我每週都拍校園花園。"},{"w":"roommate","p":"n.","d":"a person who shares a room with you","c":"室友","s":"My roommate stays up late playing games, so I wear earplugs when I need to sleep before an exam.","t":"我的室友熬夜打電動，所以考試前需要睡覺時我會戴耳塞。"},{"w":"student union","p":"n.phr.","d":"an organisation run by students to support them","c":"學生會","s":"The student union organised a free concert, and hundreds of students came to relax after their exams.","t":"學生會舉辦了一場免費音樂會，好幾百位學生考完試後來放鬆。"},{"w":"research","p":"n.","d":"careful study to discover new facts","c":"研究","s":"Her research on sleep and memory was published last year, and many teachers have shared it online.","t":"她關於睡眠與記憶的研究去年發表了，許多老師都在網路上分享。"},{"w":"laboratory","p":"n.","d":"a room where scientific experiments are done","c":"實驗室","s":"We wear safety glasses in the chemistry laboratory, because some liquids can hurt our eyes.","t":"我們在化學實驗室裡戴護目鏡，因為有些液體可能傷害眼睛。"},{"w":"fieldwork","p":"n.","d":"research done outside, in the real world","c":"田野調查；實地考察","s":"The geography students did fieldwork by the river, and they measured how fast the water was flowing.","t":"地理系學生在河邊做實地考察，並測量了水流的速度。"},{"w":"supervisor","p":"n.","d":"a teacher who guides a student's research","c":"指導教授；主管","s":"My supervisor reads every chapter of my thesis, and she gives detailed comments within a week.","t":"我的指導教授會讀我論文的每一章，並在一週內給我詳細的意見。"},{"w":"dropout","p":"n.","d":"a person who leaves school before finishing","c":"輟學生","s":"He was a high school dropout, but he went back to study at night and later became a nurse.","t":"他曾是高中輟學生，但後來回去念夜校，之後成為了護理師。"},{"w":"tertiary","p":"adj.","d":"relating to education at college or university","c":"高等（教育）的；大專的","s":"Taiwan has many tertiary institutions, so almost every high school graduate can find a place at college.","t":"台灣有許多大專院校，所以幾乎每位高中畢業生都能找到大學可念。"},{"w":"higher education","p":"n.phr.","d":"education at university or college","c":"高等教育","s":"The government spends a lot on higher education, but some people think vocational training needs more money.","t":"政府在高等教育上花了很多錢，但有些人認為職業訓練需要更多經費。"},{"w":"humanities","p":"n.","d":"subjects such as history, literature and philosophy","c":"人文學科","s":"Fewer students now choose the humanities, because many parents believe science leads to better jobs.","t":"現在選讀人文學科的學生變少了，因為許多家長認為理工科能找到較好的工作。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Gifted, Mixed-Ability & Inclusive Education 資優、混合能力與融合教育","cards":[{"w":"gifted","p":"adj.","d":"having much greater natural ability than most people","c":"有天賦的；資優的","s":"The school runs a special class for gifted children, but it also tries to keep them with friends their own age.","t":"學校為資優兒童開設特別班，但也盡量讓他們和同齡朋友待在一起。"},{"w":"talented","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural ability to do something well","c":"有才華的","s":"Many talented young musicians practise for hours every day, so they have little free time for other hobbies.","t":"許多有才華的年輕音樂家每天練習好幾個小時，所以很少有空從事其他嗜好。"},{"w":"prodigy","p":"n.","d":"a young person with extraordinary ability","c":"神童","s":"The chess prodigy beat several adult players at the age of eight, and newspapers wrote stories about him.","t":"這位西洋棋神童八歲就打敗了好幾位成人棋手，報紙紛紛報導他。"},{"w":"precocious","p":"adj.","d":"developing skills much earlier than usual","c":"早熟的","s":"She was a precocious reader who read adult novels at seven, but she sometimes felt lonely with classmates.","t":"她是個閱讀能力早熟的孩子，七歲就讀成人小說，但和同學相處時有時會感到孤單。"},{"w":"genius","p":"n.","d":"a person with extremely high intelligence or skill","c":"天才","s":"People called him a genius after he won the science prize, but he said hard work mattered more than talent.","t":"他贏得科學獎後大家稱他為天才，但他說努力比天分更重要。"},{"w":"IQ","p":"n.","d":"a number that measures a person's thinking ability","c":"智商","s":"A high IQ does not guarantee success, because skills like patience and teamwork also matter a lot.","t":"高智商並不保證成功，因為耐心和團隊合作等能力也非常重要。"},{"w":"mixed-ability","p":"adj.","d":"including students of different levels together","c":"混合能力的","s":"Teaching a mixed-ability class is challenging, so teachers often prepare easy and difficult versions of each task.","t":"教導混合能力班級很有挑戰性，所以老師常為每項任務準備簡單和困難兩種版本。"},{"w":"streaming","p":"n.","d":"putting students into classes by their ability level","c":"能力分班","s":"Some schools have stopped streaming, because weaker students in the lowest class often lose confidence.","t":"有些學校已停止能力分班，因為在最低程度班的弱勢學生常會失去自信。"},{"w":"ability grouping","p":"n.phr.","d":"forming small groups of students at similar levels","c":"能力分組","s":"Our maths teacher uses ability grouping for some activities, but she mixes the groups again for projects.","t":"我們數學老師在某些活動中採用能力分組，但做專題時她會再把各組打散混合。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"welcoming and including all kinds of people","c":"包容的；融合的","s":"An inclusive school welcomes students with disabilities, and teachers adapt lessons so everyone can take part.","t":"融合學校歡迎身心障礙學生，老師也調整課程讓每個人都能參與。"},{"w":"special needs","p":"n.phr.","d":"extra help that some students need to learn","c":"特殊需求","s":"Children with special needs may get extra time in exams, so they have a fair chance to show what they know.","t":"有特殊需求的孩子考試時可能獲得額外時間，讓他們有公平的機會展現所學。"},{"w":"learning disability","p":"n.phr.","d":"a condition that makes some kinds of learning difficult","c":"學習障礙","s":"Having a learning disability does not mean a child is not clever, and many such students go on to university.","t":"有學習障礙並不代表孩子不聰明，許多這樣的學生後來都上了大學。"},{"w":"sign language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language that uses hand movements instead of sounds","c":"手語","s":"Our class learned some basic sign language, so we could chat with a new classmate who cannot hear.","t":"我們班學了一些基本手語，這樣就能和一位聽不見的新同學聊天。"},{"w":"braille","p":"n.","d":"a system of raised dots that blind people read by touch","c":"點字","s":"The library now has textbooks in braille, so blind students can read the same lessons as everyone else.","t":"圖書館現在有點字版課本，所以視障學生能和大家讀一樣的課程。"},{"w":"deaf","p":"adj.","d":"unable to hear, or not able to hear well","c":"聾的；聽障的","s":"The deaf student follows lessons through a sign language interpreter, and she is one of the top students.","t":"這位聽障學生透過手語翻譯員上課，而且她是成績頂尖的學生之一。"},{"w":"individualised","p":"adj.","d":"planned for one particular person","c":"個別化的","s":"Each student with special needs has an individualised learning plan, and teachers review it with parents twice a year.","t":"每位特殊需求學生都有一份個別化學習計畫，老師每年和家長檢討兩次。"},{"w":"one-to-one","p":"adj.","d":"between one teacher and one student","c":"一對一的","s":"He improved quickly after a few one-to-one lessons, because the teacher could focus only on his mistakes.","t":"他上了幾堂一對一課後進步很快，因為老師能只專注在他的錯誤上。"},{"w":"slow learner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a student who needs more time to learn","c":"學習較慢的學生","s":"My father says he was a slow learner at school, but he later became an excellent engineer.","t":"我爸爸說他在學校時是個學得比較慢的學生，但後來成為了優秀的工程師。"},{"w":"struggling","p":"adj.","d":"having difficulty doing something","c":"學習困難的；吃力的","s":"Volunteers tutor struggling readers after school, and many of the children now enjoy reading picture books.","t":"志工在放學後輔導閱讀有困難的學生，許多孩子現在都喜歡讀繪本了。"},{"w":"underprivileged","p":"adj.","d":"having less money and fewer chances than most people","c":"弱勢的；貧困的","s":"The charity gives free laptops to underprivileged students, so they can join online classes at home.","t":"這個慈善團體免費提供筆電給弱勢學生，讓他們能在家參加線上課程。"},{"w":"disadvantaged","p":"adj.","d":"facing problems such as poverty that make success harder","c":"處於不利地位的","s":"Students from disadvantaged families often lack quiet places to study, so the school keeps its library open late.","t":"來自弱勢家庭的學生常缺乏安靜的讀書空間，所以學校讓圖書館開到很晚。"},{"w":"segregate","p":"v.","d":"to separate one group of people from others","c":"隔離；分開","s":"In the past many countries would segregate disabled children in separate schools, but today most try to include them.","t":"過去許多國家會把身心障礙兒童隔離在不同學校，但現在大多數國家努力讓他們融入。"},{"w":"mainstream","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and used by most people","c":"主流的；一般的","s":"Most students with mild disabilities now attend mainstream schools, and they get extra support in certain classes.","t":"大多數輕度障礙學生現在就讀一般學校，並在某些課程中獲得額外支援。"},{"w":"intensive","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of work in a short time","c":"密集的","s":"She took an intensive English course in the summer, and she studied six hours a day for four weeks.","t":"她暑假上了密集英文課，連續四週每天學習六小時。"},{"w":"expectation","p":"n.","d":"a belief about what someone should achieve","c":"期望","s":"Her parents had high expectation for her, but they never stopped her from choosing art as her major.","t":"她父母對她有很高的期望，但他們從未阻止她選擇藝術當主修。"},{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person of the same age or level as you","c":"同儕","s":"Teenagers often care more about the opinions of their peer than about what adults think.","t":"青少年往往更在意同儕的看法，而不是大人的想法。"},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good","c":"傑出的","s":"He gave an outstanding performance in the speech contest, and the judges gave him first prize.","t":"他在演講比賽中表現傑出，評審頒給他第一名。"},{"w":"elite","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the best or most powerful group","c":"菁英的；頂尖的","s":"Only a few students get into the elite science class, so competition for places is very strong.","t":"只有少數學生能進入菁英科學班，所以名額競爭非常激烈。"},{"w":"meritocracy","p":"n.","d":"a system where people succeed because of ability and hard work","c":"功績主義；菁英制度","s":"Supporters say exams create a meritocracy, but critics argue that rich families can still buy extra lessons.","t":"支持者說考試創造了功績主義的社會，但批評者認為有錢人家仍然可以花錢多補習。"},{"w":"privilege","p":"n.","d":"a special advantage that only some people have","c":"特權；優勢","s":"Studying abroad is a privilege that many families cannot afford, so scholarships are very important.","t":"出國念書是許多家庭負擔不起的特權，所以獎學金非常重要。"},{"w":"homeschool","p":"v.","d":"to teach your children at home instead of sending them to school","c":"在家自學（教育）","s":"Some parents homeschool their children because they want more freedom, but the children still need chances to make friends.","t":"有些家長讓孩子在家自學，因為他們想要更多自由，但孩子仍需要交朋友的機會。"},{"w":"numeracy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand and work with numbers","c":"數理能力；算術能力","s":"Good numeracy is needed in daily life, because we use numbers when we shop, cook and plan our time.","t":"良好的數理能力在日常生活中是必要的，因為我們購物、煮飯和規劃時間時都會用到數字。"},{"w":"socioeconomic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to social class and money","c":"社會經濟的","s":"Researchers found that socioeconomic background affects test scores, so the government gives extra money to poorer schools.","t":"研究者發現社會經濟背景會影響考試成績，所以政府給較貧困的學校額外經費。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (intellectual – administer)","cards":[{"w":"intellectual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the ability to think and understand ideas","c":"智力的；知識性的","s":"Reading widely gives children intellectual challenges, and it also helps them understand other people's feelings.","t":"廣泛閱讀給孩子帶來智力上的挑戰，也幫助他們理解別人的感受。"},{"w":"competent","p":"adj.","d":"having enough skill to do something well","c":"有能力的；稱職的","s":"After two years of practice she became a competent writer, but she still asks her teacher to check her work.","t":"經過兩年練習，她成為一位稱職的寫作者，但她仍會請老師檢查她的作品。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a job that needs special training","c":"專業的","s":"Teachers attend professional training every summer, so they can learn new ways to support their students.","t":"老師們每年暑假參加專業培訓，以便學習支持學生的新方法。"},{"w":"quote","p":"v.","d":"to repeat the exact words that someone else said or wrote","c":"引用；引述","s":"In your report you may quote a famous scientist, but you must put the words in quotation marks.","t":"在報告中你可以引用一位知名科學家的話，但必須把那段文字加上引號。"},{"w":"verbose","p":"adj.","d":"using more words than are needed","c":"冗長的；囉唆的","s":"His essay was too verbose, so the teacher asked him to cut it from 800 words to 400.","t":"他的文章太冗長了，所以老師要他從800字刪到400字。"},{"w":"version","p":"n.","d":"a slightly different form of something","c":"版本","s":"The teacher prepared an easier version of the article, so weaker readers could follow the class discussion.","t":"老師準備了這篇文章較簡單的版本，讓閱讀較弱的學生也能跟上課堂討論。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about what to do","c":"指導；輔導","s":"Students need guidance when they choose a university major, because the decision affects their future career.","t":"學生選擇大學主修時需要指導，因為這個決定會影響未來的職涯。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to understand the value of something","c":"欣賞；重視；感激","s":"I did not appreciate my history teacher at first, but now I understand how much she taught me.","t":"一開始我並不欣賞我的歷史老師，但現在我明白她教了我多少東西。"},{"w":"brief","p":"adj.","d":"short, using few words or lasting a short time","c":"簡短的","s":"Please give a brief answer to each question, because you only have twenty minutes for the whole section.","t":"請每題給出簡短的回答，因為整個部分你只有二十分鐘。"},{"w":"commentary","p":"n.","d":"a set of comments explaining or judging something","c":"評論；解說","s":"The teacher wrote a short commentary on each poem, and it helped us understand the writer's hidden meaning.","t":"老師為每首詩寫了一段簡短的評論，這幫助我們理解作者隱含的意思。"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where people discuss ideas","c":"研討會；會議","s":"Our principal attended an education conference in Singapore, and she came back with many new ideas for our school.","t":"我們校長參加了在新加坡舉辦的教育研討會，帶回許多給學校的新點子。"},{"w":"credential","p":"n.","d":"a qualification that shows you are able to do a job","c":"資歷證明；資格證書","s":"Online courses can give useful credential, but employers still want to see real skills in interviews.","t":"線上課程能提供有用的資格證明，但雇主在面試時仍想看到真正的能力。"},{"w":"acumen","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good, quick judgements","c":"敏銳；精明","s":"She showed great business acumen when she ran the school café, so the club made a big profit.","t":"她經營學校咖啡店時展現了極佳的商業敏銳度，所以社團賺了一大筆錢。"},{"w":"erudite","p":"adj.","d":"having a great deal of knowledge from reading","c":"博學的","s":"Our erudite professor can talk about almost any topic, yet he explains things in very simple language.","t":"我們那位博學的教授幾乎能談論任何話題，但他用非常簡單的語言解釋事情。"},{"w":"pedantic","p":"adj.","d":"caring too much about small details and rules","c":"迂腐的；過分拘泥細節的","s":"Some students think the teacher is pedantic about commas, but good punctuation makes writing much clearer.","t":"有些學生覺得老師對逗號過分講究，但良好的標點讓文章清楚得多。"},{"w":"didactic","p":"adj.","d":"intended to teach, often in a way that feels like a lecture","c":"說教的；教誨的","s":"The film was too didactic, so the audience felt they were being lectured instead of entertained.","t":"這部電影太說教了，所以觀眾覺得自己在被訓話而不是在娛樂。"},{"w":"formulaic","p":"adj.","d":"following a fixed pattern, with no originality","c":"公式化的","s":"Many exam essays are formulaic, because students memorise the same opening sentences and use them every time.","t":"許多考試作文都很公式化，因為學生背誦同樣的開頭句並每次都使用。"},{"w":"abide","p":"v.","d":"to accept and follow a rule or decision","c":"遵守（abide by）","s":"All candidates must abide by the exam rules, or their results may be cancelled without any warning.","t":"所有考生都必須遵守考試規則，否則成績可能會在沒有任何警告的情況下被取消。"},{"w":"abridged","p":"adj.","d":"made shorter by removing some parts","c":"刪節的；簡寫的","s":"We read an abridged version of the novel, because the original was too long for a one-month course.","t":"我們讀的是這本小說的簡寫版，因為原著對一個月的課程來說太長了。"},{"w":"absurd","p":"adj.","d":"completely silly or unreasonable","c":"荒謬的","s":"It seems absurd to give young children three hours of homework a night, and many parents have complained.","t":"讓幼童每晚寫三小時作業似乎很荒謬，許多家長已經提出抱怨。"},{"w":"accolade","p":"n.","d":"praise or an award for an achievement","c":"讚譽；獎項","s":"The teacher received the highest accolade in the city, but she said the real winners were her students.","t":"這位老師獲得全市最高的榮譽，但她說真正的贏家是她的學生。"},{"w":"accommodate","p":"v.","d":"to provide what someone needs","c":"容納；照顧到（需求）","s":"The new library can accommodate three hundred students, so it is never too crowded even during exams.","t":"新圖書館能容納三百名學生，所以即使考試期間也不會太擁擠。"},{"w":"acquaint","p":"v.","d":"to make yourself or someone familiar with something","c":"使熟悉；使認識","s":"Before the trip, the teacher wanted to acquaint us with local customs, so she showed a short video about Japan.","t":"出發前老師想讓我們熟悉當地習俗，所以她播放了一段關於日本的短片。"},{"w":"adaptable","p":"adj.","d":"able to change to suit new situations","c":"適應力強的","s":"Children are very adaptable, so most of them settle into a new school within a few weeks.","t":"孩子的適應力很強，所以大多數在幾週內就能適應新學校。"},{"w":"administer","p":"v.","d":"to organise and give something such as a test","c":"施行；實施（考試等）","s":"The teachers will administer the reading test in the morning, and the results will be ready by Friday.","t":"老師們將在早上實施閱讀測驗，結果會在星期五前出爐。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (admirable – cogent)","cards":[{"w":"admirable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect and approval","c":"令人欽佩的","s":"Her effort to learn three languages is admirable, especially because she also works part-time after school.","t":"她努力學習三種語言的精神令人欽佩，尤其是她放學後還要打工。"},{"w":"agile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move or think quickly and easily","c":"敏捷的；靈活的","s":"Chess keeps the mind agile, and many retired people play it in the park every afternoon.","t":"下西洋棋能讓頭腦保持靈活，許多退休人士每天下午都在公園下棋。"},{"w":"allot","p":"v.","d":"to give a share of time or money for a purpose","c":"分配；撥出","s":"The teacher will allot five minutes to each group, so please plan your presentation carefully.","t":"老師會分配給每組五分鐘，所以請仔細規劃你們的報告。"},{"w":"amass","p":"v.","d":"to collect a large amount of something over time","c":"累積；積聚","s":"Over four years she amass a huge collection of English novels, and she now lends them to classmates.","t":"四年來她累積了大量的英文小說，現在她把書借給同學。"},{"w":"amateur","p":"adj.","d":"doing something for enjoyment, not as a job","c":"業餘的","s":"He is only an amateur photographer, but his pictures of the school festival were printed in the newspaper.","t":"他只是個業餘攝影師，但他拍的校慶照片登上了報紙。"},{"w":"ameliorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a bad situation better","c":"改善","s":"The city built new libraries to ameliorate the lack of study space, and they are now full every weekend.","t":"市政府蓋了新圖書館來改善讀書空間不足的問題，現在每個週末都座無虛席。"},{"w":"amenable","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept or be influenced by ideas","c":"願意接受的","s":"The principal was amenable to the students' suggestion, so the school changed the lunch break to one hour.","t":"校長願意接受學生的建議，所以學校把午休改成一小時。"},{"w":"antiquated","p":"adj.","d":"old-fashioned and no longer suitable","c":"過時的；老舊的","s":"The school's computers are antiquated, so students often bring their own laptops to finish projects.","t":"學校的電腦老舊過時，所以學生常自己帶筆電來完成專題。"},{"w":"apt","p":"adj.","d":"suitable or right for a situation","c":"恰當的","s":"\"Practice makes perfect\" was an apt title for her speech, because she talked about learning the violin.","t":"「熟能生巧」是她演講恰當的標題，因為她談的是學小提琴。"},{"w":"archaic","p":"adj.","d":"very old and no longer used","c":"古老的；已不使用的","s":"Shakespeare uses many archaic words, so students often need notes to understand his famous plays today.","t":"莎士比亞使用許多古老的字詞，所以現今學生常需要註解才能理解他的名劇。"},{"w":"ardent","p":"adj.","d":"very enthusiastic and passionate","c":"熱心的；熱烈的","s":"My uncle is an ardent supporter of free education, and he volunteers at a reading centre every Sunday.","t":"我叔叔是免費教育的熱烈支持者，他每個星期天都在閱讀中心當志工。"},{"w":"assiduous","p":"adj.","d":"working very carefully and with great effort","c":"勤勉的；刻苦的","s":"She was an assiduous student who checked every answer twice, so she rarely made careless mistakes.","t":"她是個勤勉的學生，每個答案都檢查兩次，所以很少粗心犯錯。"},{"w":"austere","p":"adj.","d":"very plain and simple, without comfort","c":"簡樸的；樸素的","s":"The old boarding school had austere rooms with only a bed and a desk, but the students did not complain.","t":"那所舊寄宿學校的房間很簡樸，只有一張床和一張書桌，但學生們沒有抱怨。"},{"w":"avid","p":"adj.","d":"very keen and enthusiastic about something","c":"熱衷的","s":"He is an avid reader of science fiction, and he borrows at least three books from the library each week.","t":"他是科幻小說的熱衷讀者，每週至少從圖書館借三本書。"},{"w":"axiom","p":"n.","d":"a statement accepted as true without needing proof","c":"公理；格言","s":"It is an axiom in education that children learn best when they feel safe, so schools must stop bullying.","t":"孩子在感到安全時學得最好，這是教育界的公理，所以學校必須杜絕霸凌。"},{"w":"belittle","p":"v.","d":"to make someone or something seem unimportant","c":"貶低；輕視","s":"Good teachers never belittle students' questions, because even simple questions can lead to deep learning.","t":"好老師從不輕視學生的問題，因為即使是簡單的問題也可能帶來深入的學習。"},{"w":"brevity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of using few words","c":"簡潔；簡短","s":"The judges praised the speech for its brevity, because she made three strong points in only two minutes.","t":"評審稱讚這篇演講簡潔，因為她只用兩分鐘就提出三個有力的論點。"},{"w":"bureaucracy","p":"n.","d":"a system with many complicated official rules","c":"官僚制度；繁文縟節","s":"Teachers complain about too much bureaucracy, because they spend hours filling in forms instead of preparing lessons.","t":"老師們抱怨太多繁文縟節，因為他們花好幾個小時填表格而不是備課。"},{"w":"calibre","p":"n.","d":"the level of quality or ability","c":"才幹；水準","s":"The school attracts teachers of high calibre, so its students often win national science prizes.","t":"這所學校吸引了高水準的教師，所以學生常贏得全國科學獎項。"},{"w":"categorical","p":"adj.","d":"very clear and certain, with no doubt","c":"絕對的；明確的","s":"The principal gave a categorical answer that phones would not be allowed in class, so nobody argued.","t":"校長明確表示上課時不准使用手機，所以沒有人爭論。"},{"w":"censure","p":"v.","d":"to criticise someone strongly and officially","c":"譴責；責難","s":"The education board censure the school for hiding its exam problems, and the principal later resigned.","t":"教育局譴責這所學校隱瞞考試問題，校長後來辭職了。"},{"w":"cerebral","p":"adj.","d":"needing careful thought rather than feelings","c":"需要動腦的；理性的","s":"Chess is a very cerebral game, but young children can still enjoy it with simple rules.","t":"西洋棋是非常需要動腦的遊戲，但幼童仍能用簡單的規則樂在其中。"},{"w":"chronological","p":"adj.","d":"arranged in the order in which events happened","c":"按時間順序的","s":"Put the events in chronological order, and then write a short paragraph about the most important one.","t":"把事件按時間順序排列，然後針對最重要的事件寫一小段。"},{"w":"coerce","p":"v.","d":"to force someone to do something they do not want to do","c":"強迫；脅迫","s":"Parents should not coerce children into studying medicine, because forced choices often lead to unhappy careers.","t":"父母不應強迫孩子讀醫科，因為被迫的選擇常導致不快樂的職涯。"},{"w":"cogent","p":"adj.","d":"clear, logical and able to persuade people","c":"有說服力的","s":"Her argument was cogent and well organised, so the debate judges gave her team the highest score.","t":"她的論點有說服力且條理分明，所以辯論評審給她的隊伍最高分。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (collate – doctrine)","cards":[{"w":"collate","p":"v.","d":"to collect and arrange information in order","c":"整理；彙整","s":"The class leader will collate everyone's answers to the survey, and then she will share the results on Monday.","t":"班長會彙整大家的問卷答案，然後在星期一分享結果。"},{"w":"colloquial","p":"adj.","d":"used in informal conversation, not formal writing","c":"口語的","s":"\"Gonna\" is a colloquial word, so you should not use it in an academic essay or a formal email.","t":"gonna 是口語用字，所以不應用在學術文章或正式電子郵件中。"},{"w":"commensurate","p":"adj.","d":"matching in size, amount or level","c":"相稱的；相當的","s":"Teachers want salaries commensurate with their long working hours, but the budget has not increased for years.","t":"老師們希望薪水與長工時相稱，但預算已經好幾年沒有增加。"},{"w":"compartmentalise","p":"v.","d":"to divide things into separate parts","c":"把…分隔開；區隔處理","s":"Schools often compartmentalise knowledge into separate subjects, but real problems need science, maths and language together.","t":"學校常把知識分隔成各別科目，但真實的問題需要同時運用科學、數學和語言。"},{"w":"concerted","p":"adj.","d":"done by people working together with determination","c":"共同的；齊心協力的","s":"Parents and teachers made a concerted effort to reduce phone use, and students now talk more during breaks.","t":"家長和老師齊心協力減少手機使用，現在學生下課時聊天變多了。"},{"w":"condense","p":"v.","d":"to make a text shorter but keep the main ideas","c":"濃縮；精簡","s":"Try to condense your notes onto one page, because it is easier to review a short summary before the test.","t":"試著把筆記濃縮成一頁，因為考前複習簡短的摘要比較容易。"},{"w":"conversant","p":"adj.","d":"having knowledge of something","c":"熟悉的；精通的","s":"Most students are conversant with social media, but many still do not know how to check facts online.","t":"大多數學生熟悉社群媒體，但許多人仍不知道如何在網路上查證事實。"},{"w":"copious","p":"adj.","d":"in large amounts","c":"大量的；豐富的","s":"She took copious notes during the lecture, so she could explain every detail to her sick friend later.","t":"她上課時做了大量筆記，所以之後能向生病的朋友解釋每個細節。"},{"w":"credence","p":"n.","d":"belief that something is true","c":"相信；可信度","s":"The new study gives credence to the idea that sleep helps memory, so schools may start classes later.","t":"這項新研究為「睡眠有助記憶」的說法增添了可信度，所以學校可能會延後上課時間。"},{"w":"critique","p":"v.","d":"to judge something carefully, showing good and bad points","c":"評論；評析","s":"In art class we critique each other's paintings, but we must always begin with something positive.","t":"美術課上我們互相評析彼此的畫作，但一定要先從優點說起。"},{"w":"cursory","p":"adj.","d":"done quickly without paying attention to details","c":"粗略的；草率的","s":"He gave the article only a cursory glance, so he missed the most important point in the last paragraph.","t":"他只是粗略看了一眼那篇文章，所以錯過了最後一段最重要的重點。"},{"w":"debilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone or something very weak","c":"使衰弱","s":"Lack of sleep can debilitate students during exam season, so doctors advise at least seven hours a night.","t":"睡眠不足會在考試期間使學生虛弱，所以醫生建議每晚至少睡七小時。"},{"w":"decipher","p":"v.","d":"to work out the meaning of something difficult to read","c":"辨認；解讀","s":"The teacher could not decipher his messy handwriting, so she asked him to type his essay next time.","t":"老師無法辨認他潦草的字跡，所以要他下次把作文打字。"},{"w":"deference","p":"n.","d":"polite respect for someone's opinion or position","c":"尊重；敬意","s":"In many Asian classrooms students show deference to teachers, but this can make them afraid to ask questions.","t":"在許多亞洲教室裡學生對老師表現敬意，但這可能使他們不敢發問。"},{"w":"delve","p":"v.","d":"to search deeply for information","c":"深入探究","s":"For her project she delve into old newspapers, and she discovered how her school was founded in 1920.","t":"為了專題她深入研究舊報紙，發現了她的學校在1920年是如何創立的。"},{"w":"demeanour","p":"n.","d":"the way a person behaves or looks","c":"舉止；態度","s":"The examiner had a calm demeanour, so the nervous students relaxed as soon as the interview started.","t":"主考官舉止沉穩，所以緊張的學生在面試一開始就放鬆了。"},{"w":"demystify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand","c":"使易懂；揭開神秘面紗","s":"The workshop aims to demystify university applications, so parents can help their children without paying agents.","t":"這個工作坊旨在讓大學申請流程變得易懂，讓家長不用花錢請代辦也能協助孩子。"},{"w":"denounce","p":"v.","d":"to criticise something strongly in public","c":"公開譴責","s":"Many teachers denounce the plan to cut art classes, and they started a campaign to protect them.","t":"許多老師公開譴責刪減美術課的計畫，並發起運動來保護這些課程。"},{"w":"deride","p":"v.","d":"to laugh at someone in an unkind way","c":"嘲笑","s":"Other students used to deride his accent, but now he speaks three languages and works as an interpreter.","t":"以前其他學生常嘲笑他的口音，但現在他會說三種語言並擔任口譯員。"},{"w":"desirable","p":"adj.","d":"worth having or wanting","c":"令人嚮往的；理想的","s":"Good communication skills are highly desirable in any job, so schools should give students chances to speak.","t":"良好的溝通能力在任何工作中都非常理想，所以學校應該給學生說話的機會。"},{"w":"dexterity","p":"n.","d":"skill in using your hands or mind","c":"靈巧；熟練","s":"Playing the piano improves finger dexterity, and it also trains children to read music quickly.","t":"彈鋼琴能提升手指的靈巧度，也訓練孩子快速讀譜。"},{"w":"digress","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something not connected to the main topic","c":"離題","s":"Our history teacher often digress to tell funny stories, but we always learn something from them.","t":"我們的歷史老師常常離題講有趣的故事，但我們總能從中學到東西。"},{"w":"disseminate","p":"v.","d":"to spread information widely","c":"傳播；散布","s":"The school uses an app to disseminate news to parents, so nobody misses important dates any more.","t":"學校用一款應用程式向家長傳播消息，所以再也沒有人錯過重要日期。"},{"w":"distil","p":"v.","d":"to take the most important ideas from something","c":"提煉；萃取精華","s":"The teacher helped us distil the long article into five key points, and we wrote them on a poster.","t":"老師幫我們把那篇長文章提煉成五個重點，並寫在海報上。"},{"w":"doctrine","p":"n.","d":"a set of beliefs taught by a group","c":"學說；教義","s":"The old doctrine that children should be seen and not heard is disappearing, and students now share opinions freely.","t":"「小孩有耳無嘴」的舊觀念正在消失，現在學生可以自由分享意見。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (dogmatic – hone)","cards":[{"w":"dogmatic","p":"adj.","d":"sure that your beliefs are right and refusing other ideas","c":"武斷的；教條的","s":"A dogmatic teacher may stop students from thinking critically, because they learn that only one answer is accepted.","t":"教條式的老師可能會阻礙學生批判思考，因為他們學到只有一個答案被接受。"},{"w":"eclectic","p":"adj.","d":"including ideas or styles from many different sources","c":"兼容並蓄的；多元的","s":"She has an eclectic taste in books, so her shelves hold poetry, comics, history and science fiction.","t":"她閱讀品味多元，所以書架上有詩集、漫畫、歷史和科幻小說。"},{"w":"egalitarian","p":"adj.","d":"believing everyone should have equal rights and chances","c":"平等主義的","s":"Finland has a very egalitarian school system, and almost every child attends a free local school.","t":"芬蘭的學校制度非常平等，幾乎每個孩子都就讀免費的社區學校。"},{"w":"elucidate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something clearly","c":"闡明；解釋清楚","s":"The professor used a simple diagram to elucidate the theory, and suddenly the whole class understood it.","t":"教授用一張簡單的圖表來闡明這個理論，全班突然都懂了。"},{"w":"eminent","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected in a particular field","c":"傑出的；著名的","s":"An eminent scientist visited our school, and she encouraged girls to study physics and engineering.","t":"一位著名的科學家來訪我們學校，並鼓勵女生攻讀物理和工程。"},{"w":"emphatic","p":"adj.","d":"said with force to show something is important","c":"強調的；斷然的","s":"Her answer was emphatic: she would not let her son quit school, even though he wanted to become a gamer.","t":"她的回答很斷然：即使兒子想當電玩選手，她也不會讓他休學。"},{"w":"encapsulate","p":"v.","d":"to express the main idea in a short way","c":"概括；簡述","s":"Your title should encapsulate the main idea of your essay, so the reader knows what to expect.","t":"你的標題應該概括文章的主旨，讓讀者知道會讀到什麼。"},{"w":"endow","p":"v.","d":"to give a large amount of money to a school or other organisation","c":"捐贈；資助","s":"A former student endow the library with a million dollars, and it now has a new reading room.","t":"一位校友捐贈了一百萬元給圖書館，現在圖書館有了一間新的閱覽室。"},{"w":"engender","p":"v.","d":"to cause a feeling or situation to exist","c":"引起；產生","s":"Constant comparison with classmates can engender jealousy, so parents should focus on their child's own progress.","t":"不斷和同學比較可能會引起嫉妒，所以家長應關注孩子自身的進步。"},{"w":"enumerate","p":"v.","d":"to name things one by one in a list","c":"列舉","s":"The teacher asked us to enumerate the causes of the war, and then we discussed which one was most important.","t":"老師要我們列舉戰爭的起因，然後我們討論哪一個最重要。"},{"w":"esoteric","p":"adj.","d":"understood only by a small group of experts","c":"深奧的；冷門難懂的","s":"The lecture was too esoteric for first-year students, so many of them stopped taking notes after ten minutes.","t":"這堂課對大一學生來說太深奧了，所以很多人十分鐘後就不再做筆記。"},{"w":"espouse","p":"v.","d":"to support an idea or belief","c":"擁護；支持","s":"Many modern teachers espouse learning through play, and they believe children remember more when they have fun.","t":"許多現代老師擁護從遊戲中學習，他們相信孩子在快樂時記得更多。"},{"w":"exacting","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of care, effort and skill","c":"要求嚴格的；費力的","s":"The music academy has exacting standards, so students practise for many hours before each audition.","t":"這所音樂學院標準嚴格，所以學生在每次試鏡前都要練習好幾個小時。"},{"w":"exasperate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very annoyed","c":"激怒；使惱火","s":"Students who chat during tests exasperate the teacher, so she now moves them to the front row.","t":"考試時聊天的學生惹惱了老師，所以她現在把他們移到第一排。"},{"w":"exempt","p":"adj.","d":"not required to do something that others must do","c":"被免除的","s":"Students with a high listening score are exempt from the extra class, so they can use the time for self-study.","t":"聽力分數高的學生免上加強課，所以他們能用這段時間自修。"},{"w":"expound","p":"v.","d":"to explain an idea in detail","c":"詳細闡述","s":"The guest speaker expound on the history of Taiwanese education, and he answered questions for an hour afterwards.","t":"客座講者詳細闡述台灣教育的歷史，之後還回答了一個小時的問題。"},{"w":"facile","p":"adj.","d":"too simple and not showing careful thought","c":"膚淺的；輕率的","s":"Saying that students are lazy is a facile explanation, because many of them are simply tired from long school days.","t":"說學生懶惰是膚淺的解釋，因為他們很多人只是被漫長的上學日累壞了。"},{"w":"fallible","p":"adj.","d":"able to make mistakes","c":"會犯錯的","s":"Teachers are fallible like everyone else, so they should admit their mistakes in front of students.","t":"老師和其他人一樣會犯錯，所以應該在學生面前承認錯誤。"},{"w":"frivolous","p":"adj.","d":"not serious or important","c":"輕浮的；無關緊要的","s":"Some parents see drama club as frivolous, but it builds confidence and teamwork that are useful in any job.","t":"有些家長認為戲劇社無關緊要，但它培養的自信和團隊合作在任何工作中都很有用。"},{"w":"galvanise","p":"v.","d":"to shock or excite someone into taking action","c":"激勵；促使行動","s":"The flood in the village galvanise students to raise money, and they collected enough to rebuild the school library.","t":"村莊的水災激勵學生募款，他們募到足夠的錢重建學校圖書館。"},{"w":"garner","p":"v.","d":"to collect or gain something such as support","c":"獲得；贏得","s":"Her speech about mental health garner a lot of support, and the school agreed to hire another counsellor.","t":"她關於心理健康的演講贏得大量支持，學校同意再聘一位輔導老師。"},{"w":"glean","p":"v.","d":"to collect information slowly, in small amounts","c":"蒐集（資訊）；點滴獲得","s":"I glean useful tips from older students, and they helped me prepare for my university interview.","t":"我從學長姊那裡蒐集到許多有用的建議，它們幫助我準備大學面試。"},{"w":"grapple","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to deal with a difficult problem","c":"努力解決；奮力應付","s":"Many schools grapple with how to use AI tools fairly, but there are still no clear national rules.","t":"許多學校正努力解決如何公平使用人工智慧工具的問題，但至今仍沒有明確的全國規範。"},{"w":"haphazard","p":"adj.","d":"not planned or organised","c":"雜亂無章的；隨意的","s":"His haphazard way of studying wasted a lot of time, so his tutor helped him make a weekly plan.","t":"他雜亂無章的讀書方式浪費了很多時間，所以家教幫他制定了每週計畫。"},{"w":"hone","p":"v.","d":"to improve a skill through practice","c":"磨練","s":"She joined the debate club to hone her speaking skills, and now she is confident in every presentation.","t":"她加入辯論社來磨練口語能力，現在她在每次報告中都充滿自信。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (idiosyncratic – maxim)","cards":[{"w":"idiosyncratic","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and typical of one particular person","c":"獨特的；特立獨行的","s":"The professor has an idiosyncratic teaching style, but students love his classes because they are never boring.","t":"這位教授的教學風格很獨特，但學生喜歡他的課，因為從不無聊。"},{"w":"illustrious","p":"adj.","d":"famous and admired because of great achievements","c":"傑出的；顯赫的","s":"The university has an illustrious history, and several of its former students have won Nobel Prizes.","t":"這所大學有輝煌的歷史，好幾位校友都得過諾貝爾獎。"},{"w":"impart","p":"v.","d":"to pass knowledge or skills to someone","c":"傳授；傳遞","s":"Good teachers do more than impart facts, because they also show students how to think for themselves.","t":"好老師不只是傳授事實，他們也教學生如何獨立思考。"},{"w":"impoverished","p":"adj.","d":"very poor","c":"貧困的","s":"Children in impoverished villages often walk for hours to school, but many of them still dream of going to university.","t":"貧困村莊的孩子常要走好幾個小時去上學，但他們許多人仍夢想上大學。"},{"w":"incongruous","p":"adj.","d":"strange because it does not fit the situation","c":"不協調的；格格不入的","s":"His bright red suit looked incongruous at the serious graduation ceremony, and many people turned to stare at him.","t":"他那套鮮紅色西裝在莊重的畢業典禮上顯得格格不入，許多人轉頭盯著他看。"},{"w":"inconsequential","p":"adj.","d":"not important","c":"無關緊要的","s":"Don't waste time on inconsequential details in the exam, because the main argument is worth most of the marks.","t":"考試時別把時間浪費在無關緊要的細節上，因為主要論點佔了大部分的分數。"},{"w":"indoctrinate","p":"v.","d":"to teach people to accept beliefs without questioning them","c":"灌輸（思想）","s":"Schools should not indoctrinate students with one political view, but should help them compare different opinions.","t":"學校不應向學生灌輸單一政治觀點，而應幫助他們比較不同意見。"},{"w":"inexorable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to stop","c":"無法阻擋的","s":"The inexorable rise of online learning has changed schools, and even grandparents now take courses on their phones.","t":"線上學習勢不可擋的興起改變了學校，連祖父母現在都用手機上課。"},{"w":"instigate","p":"v.","d":"to start an action or event","c":"發起；促成","s":"The students instigate a campaign to save the old school tree, and the city finally agreed to protect it.","t":"學生們發起了一場拯救校園老樹的運動，市政府最後同意保護它。"},{"w":"ingenuity","p":"n.","d":"skill in thinking of clever new ideas","c":"巧思；創造力","s":"The robot team showed great ingenuity, because they built their machine from old bicycles and plastic bottles.","t":"機器人隊展現了極大的巧思，因為他們用舊腳踏車和塑膠瓶打造機器。"},{"w":"instrumental","p":"adj.","d":"very important in making something happen","c":"起重要作用的","s":"My English teacher was instrumental in helping me win the scholarship, so I sent her a thank-you card.","t":"我的英文老師在幫助我贏得獎學金這件事上功不可沒，所以我寄了一張感謝卡給她。"},{"w":"intelligible","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to be understood","c":"可理解的；清楚易懂的","s":"Your accent does not matter much, as long as your speech is intelligible and your ideas are clear.","t":"你的口音不太重要，只要你的話語清楚易懂、想法清晰就好。"},{"w":"interdisciplinary","p":"adj.","d":"involving two or more subjects","c":"跨學科的","s":"Our interdisciplinary project combined history and art, so we painted a mural about our town's past.","t":"我們的跨學科專題結合了歷史與藝術，所以我們畫了一幅關於小鎮過去的壁畫。"},{"w":"jargon","p":"n.","d":"special words used by a group that others find hard to understand","c":"術語；行話","s":"The report was full of education jargon, so many parents could not understand the new policy.","t":"這份報告充滿教育術語，所以許多家長看不懂新政策。"},{"w":"juxtapose","p":"v.","d":"to put two things side by side to compare them","c":"並列；並置","s":"The writer juxtapose a rich school and a poor school, and the contrast made readers think about fairness.","t":"作者把一所富裕學校和一所貧窮學校並列比較，這種對比讓讀者思考公平問題。"},{"w":"laborious","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time and effort","c":"費力的；辛苦的","s":"Copying notes by hand is laborious, but some studies show it helps students remember more.","t":"用手抄筆記很費力，但有些研究顯示它能幫助學生記住更多。"},{"w":"laudable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving praise","c":"值得稱讚的","s":"The plan to give every child a free breakfast is laudable, but the city still needs to find the money.","t":"讓每個孩子都有免費早餐的計畫值得稱讚，但市政府仍需籌措經費。"},{"w":"lax","p":"adj.","d":"not strict enough","c":"鬆散的；不嚴格的","s":"Security at the exam centre was lax, so some students brought their phones into the room.","t":"考場的安全管理很鬆散，所以有些學生把手機帶進了考場。"},{"w":"legible","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to read","c":"字跡清楚的；易讀的","s":"Please make your handwriting legible, because the examiners cannot give marks for words they cannot read.","t":"請把字寫得清楚易讀，因為閱卷人無法為看不懂的字給分。"},{"w":"literal","p":"adj.","d":"using the basic meaning of a word","c":"字面上的","s":"A literal translation of an idiom often sounds strange, so translators look for a phrase with the same feeling.","t":"成語的字面翻譯常常聽起來很奇怪，所以譯者會找有相同感覺的說法。"},{"w":"lofty","p":"adj.","d":"very high, noble or ambitious","c":"崇高的；遠大的","s":"The school has lofty goals for every student, but some teachers worry that the targets are unrealistic.","t":"學校為每位學生設定了遠大的目標，但有些老師擔心這些目標不切實際。"},{"w":"longitudinal","p":"adj.","d":"studying the same people over a long time","c":"縱貫的；長期追蹤的","s":"A longitudinal study followed 1,000 children for twenty years, and it found that reading at home predicted later success.","t":"一項長期追蹤研究追蹤了一千名兒童二十年，發現在家閱讀能預測日後的成功。"},{"w":"malleable","p":"adj.","d":"easily changed or influenced","c":"可塑的；易受影響的","s":"Young minds are malleable, so the habits children form at school can last for their whole lives.","t":"年輕的心智是可塑的，所以孩子在學校養成的習慣可能維持一輩子。"},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adj.","d":"required by law or rules","c":"強制的；義務的","s":"Swimming lessons are mandatory in many schools in Taiwan, because the island is surrounded by sea.","t":"游泳課在台灣許多學校是必修的，因為這座島四面環海。"},{"w":"maxim","p":"n.","d":"a short saying that gives a rule for behaviour","c":"格言；座右銘","s":"My grandfather's favourite maxim was \"Never stop learning\", and he took a computer class at eighty.","t":"我祖父最喜歡的格言是「學無止境」，他八十歲時還去上電腦課。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (methodical – propel)","cards":[{"w":"methodical","p":"adj.","d":"doing things carefully in a planned order","c":"有條不紊的","s":"Lisa is very methodical when she studies, so she always finishes her review a week before the test.","t":"麗莎讀書時非常有條不紊，所以她總在考試前一週就完成複習。"},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"not very large; or not talking much about your success","c":"適度的；謙虛的","s":"The new rule brought only a modest improvement in reading scores, but teachers hope it will grow over time.","t":"新規定只帶來些微的閱讀成績進步，但老師們希望它會隨時間擴大。"},{"w":"myopic","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking about the future","c":"短視的","s":"Cutting the library budget is a myopic decision, because reading skills affect every other subject.","t":"刪減圖書館預算是短視的決定，因為閱讀能力會影響其他每一科。"},{"w":"naive","p":"adj.","d":"lacking experience and too ready to believe things","c":"天真的","s":"It is naive to believe everything you read online, so students must learn to check sources.","t":"相信網路上讀到的每件事是很天真的，所以學生必須學會查證來源。"},{"w":"negligent","p":"adj.","d":"not taking enough care","c":"疏忽的；失職的","s":"The school was found negligent after a student was hurt in the lab, because no teacher was watching.","t":"一名學生在實驗室受傷後，學校被認定疏失，因為當時沒有老師在場看管。"},{"w":"nominal","p":"adj.","d":"very small, much less than the real value","c":"象徵性的；極少的","s":"The museum charges students only a nominal fee, so whole classes can visit on school trips.","t":"博物館只向學生收取象徵性的費用，所以整班都能在校外教學時參觀。"},{"w":"onerous","p":"adj.","d":"difficult and heavy to deal with","c":"繁重的","s":"The onerous paperwork for studying abroad took her weeks, but her visa finally arrived in July.","t":"出國留學的繁重文件花了她好幾週，但她的簽證終於在七月寄到了。"},{"w":"opaque","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to understand; not clear","c":"不透明的；難懂的","s":"The scoring system was opaque, so parents asked the school to explain how the results were calculated.","t":"評分制度不透明，所以家長要求學校說明成績是如何計算的。"},{"w":"ostensibly","p":"adv.","d":"seeming to be true, but perhaps not really","c":"表面上","s":"The new test is ostensibly about creativity, but many students say it still rewards memorising answers.","t":"新測驗表面上是考創造力，但許多學生說它仍然獎勵背答案。"},{"w":"outmoded","p":"adj.","d":"no longer fashionable or useful","c":"過時的","s":"Some teaching methods are outmoded, so the government is training teachers to use more discussion in class.","t":"有些教學方法已經過時，所以政府正在訓練老師在課堂上多採用討論。"},{"w":"overhaul","p":"v.","d":"to change a system completely to improve it","c":"徹底檢修；全面改革","s":"The ministry plans to overhaul the exam system, but teachers want more time to prepare for the changes.","t":"教育部計畫全面改革考試制度，但老師們希望有更多時間準備這些改變。"},{"w":"oversee","p":"v.","d":"to watch and organise work to check it is done well","c":"監督；督導","s":"A senior teacher will oversee the science fair, so every project is checked for safety first.","t":"一位資深老師將督導科展，所以每件作品都會先接受安全檢查。"},{"w":"peculiar","p":"adj.","d":"strange or unusual","c":"奇怪的；特殊的","s":"The new student had a peculiar habit of reading while walking, and he once walked into a door.","t":"那位新同學有邊走路邊看書的奇怪習慣，有一次還撞上了門。"},{"w":"perplex","p":"v.","d":"to make someone confused","c":"使困惑","s":"The last question perplex most students, because it used a word that nobody had seen before.","t":"最後一題讓大部分學生很困惑，因為它用了一個沒人見過的字。"},{"w":"plethora","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount, often too much","c":"過多；大量","s":"There is a plethora of learning apps online, so it is hard for parents to choose the best one.","t":"網路上有大量學習應用程式，所以家長很難選出最好的一個。"},{"w":"polarise","p":"v.","d":"to divide people into two opposing groups","c":"使兩極化","s":"The debate about school uniforms tends to polarise parents, because some see them as fair and others as old-fashioned.","t":"關於校服的爭論往往使家長意見兩極化，因為有些人認為它公平，有些人認為它過時。"},{"w":"postulate","p":"v.","d":"to suggest an idea as a basis for a theory","c":"假定；提出（理論）","s":"Some researchers postulate that bilingual children solve problems faster, but more evidence is needed before schools change.","t":"有些研究者假定雙語兒童解決問題更快，但在學校做出改變之前，仍需要更多證據。"},{"w":"precedent","p":"n.","d":"an earlier event used as an example for later decisions","c":"先例","s":"Letting one student retake the test would set a precedent, so the teacher refused all similar requests.","t":"讓一位學生重考會開先例，所以老師拒絕了所有類似的要求。"},{"w":"preconception","p":"n.","d":"an idea formed before you have enough information","c":"先入之見；成見","s":"Many people have a preconception that vocational schools are for weak students, but this is often untrue.","t":"許多人有個成見，認為技職學校是給程度差的學生念的，但這常常不是事實。"},{"w":"predecessor","p":"n.","d":"the person who had a job before someone else","c":"前任","s":"The new principal kept many of her predecessor ideas, but she also added a reading hour every morning.","t":"新校長保留了許多前任校長的想法，但她也增加了每天早上的閱讀時間。"},{"w":"premature","p":"adj.","d":"happening too early","c":"過早的","s":"It is premature to judge the new curriculum after one year, so researchers want to wait for more data.","t":"一年後就評斷新課綱還太早，所以研究者想等更多資料。"},{"w":"presuppose","p":"v.","d":"to assume something is true before you begin","c":"預先假定；以…為前提","s":"The question presuppose that all students have a computer at home, but many families do not own one.","t":"這個題目預設所有學生家裡都有電腦，但許多家庭並沒有。"},{"w":"prestigious","p":"adj.","d":"respected and admired as very good","c":"有聲望的；名聲顯赫的","s":"She was accepted by a prestigious university in London, and her whole family celebrated at a restaurant.","t":"她被倫敦一所名校錄取，全家人在餐廳慶祝。"},{"w":"propagate","p":"v.","d":"to spread ideas or beliefs to many people","c":"傳播；宣揚","s":"Social media can propagate false ideas about learning, so teachers explain what the research really says.","t":"社群媒體可能散播關於學習的錯誤觀念，所以老師會解釋研究真正的結論。"},{"w":"propel","p":"v.","d":"to push or drive someone forward","c":"推動；推進","s":"Winning the science contest propel her into the national team, and she later studied physics abroad.","t":"贏得科學競賽推動她進入國家隊，她後來出國攻讀物理。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (prospective – dissuade)","cards":[{"w":"prospective","p":"adj.","d":"expected to become something in the future","c":"未來的；預期的","s":"The university held an open day for prospective students, and they toured the labs and dormitories.","t":"大學為未來的學生舉辦了開放日，他們參觀了實驗室和宿舍。"},{"w":"punitive","p":"adj.","d":"intended as punishment","c":"懲罰性的","s":"Many experts say punitive rules do not stop bullying, so schools should also teach empathy and kindness.","t":"許多專家說懲罰性的規定無法阻止霸凌，所以學校也應該教導同理心和善良。"},{"w":"quintessential","p":"adj.","d":"being the most typical example of something","c":"典型的；精髓的","s":"Night markets are a quintessential part of Taiwanese life, so exchange students always ask to visit one.","t":"夜市是台灣生活最典型的一部分，所以交換學生總是要求去逛。"},{"w":"reform","p":"n.","d":"a change made to improve a system","c":"改革","s":"The education reform gave students more elective courses, but some parents worry about university entrance.","t":"這次教育改革給了學生更多選修課，但有些家長擔心升大學的問題。"},{"w":"relegate","p":"v.","d":"to move someone or something to a less important position","c":"降級；貶至次要地位","s":"Many schools relegate art and music to one hour a week, because they focus on exam subjects.","t":"許多學校把美術和音樂降為每週一小時，因為他們專注在考試科目上。"},{"w":"sanction","p":"n.","d":"official permission or approval","c":"批准；認可","s":"The club cannot hold the overnight event without the school's sanction, so the leaders wrote a formal request.","t":"沒有學校的批准，社團不能舉辦過夜活動，所以幹部寫了正式申請。"},{"w":"seminal","p":"adj.","d":"very important and influencing later work","c":"開創性的；影響深遠的","s":"Her seminal research on how children learn to read changed teaching methods around the world.","t":"她關於兒童如何學習閱讀的開創性研究改變了全世界的教學方法。"},{"w":"solicit","p":"v.","d":"to ask for something such as money or opinions","c":"徵求；請求","s":"The principal solicit ideas from students about the new canteen menu, and she received over five hundred replies.","t":"校長向學生徵求新餐廳菜單的點子，並收到超過五百份回覆。"},{"w":"streamline","p":"v.","d":"to make a system simpler and more efficient","c":"精簡；使更有效率","s":"The university wants to streamline its application process, so students will fill in one online form instead of five.","t":"大學想簡化申請流程，所以學生只需填寫一份線上表格而不是五份。"},{"w":"supersede","p":"v.","d":"to replace something older or less useful","c":"取代","s":"Tablets have not completely supersede paper books, and many students still prefer printed pages for long reading.","t":"平板電腦並沒有完全取代紙本書，許多學生長篇閱讀時仍偏好印刷書頁。"},{"w":"tacit","p":"adj.","d":"understood without being said","c":"心照不宣的；默許的","s":"There was a tacit agreement that nobody would talk during the reading hour, so the room was completely silent.","t":"大家有個心照不宣的共識，閱讀時間沒有人說話，所以教室裡一片寂靜。"},{"w":"tenet","p":"n.","d":"a main principle or belief","c":"原則；信條","s":"A key tenet of the school is respect for others, and teachers remind students of it every day.","t":"這所學校的一項重要信條是尊重他人，老師每天都提醒學生。"},{"w":"transcend","p":"v.","d":"to go beyond the usual limits of something","c":"超越","s":"Music can transcend language barriers, so the international students soon sang together in the school choir.","t":"音樂能超越語言障礙，所以國際學生很快就在學校合唱團裡一起唱歌。"},{"w":"underpin","p":"v.","d":"to give strong support to an idea or system","c":"支撐；作為…的基礎","s":"Strong reading skills underpin success in every subject, so the school gives extra help to weak readers.","t":"紮實的閱讀能力是各科成功的基礎，所以學校給閱讀較弱的學生額外協助。"},{"w":"utilitarian","p":"adj.","d":"designed to be useful rather than beautiful","c":"實用的；功利的","s":"The old classroom was utilitarian and grey, but the students decorated it with posters and plants.","t":"那間舊教室只講實用又灰暗，但學生們用海報和植物把它佈置起來。"},{"w":"venerable","p":"adj.","d":"respected because of age or experience","c":"德高望重的；歷史悠久的","s":"The venerable school celebrated its hundredth birthday, and former students came back from all over the world.","t":"這所歷史悠久的學校慶祝百年校慶，校友們從世界各地回來。"},{"w":"vindicate","p":"v.","d":"to prove that someone was right","c":"證明…是正確的","s":"The excellent results vindicate the teacher's new method, so other schools now want to try it too.","t":"優異的成績證明這位老師的新方法是對的，所以其他學校現在也想嘗試。"},{"w":"wholesome","p":"adj.","d":"good for your health or your moral character","c":"有益身心的","s":"The school serves wholesome lunches with rice, vegetables and fish, and fried food is only offered once a week.","t":"學校供應米飯、蔬菜和魚等有益健康的午餐，而油炸食物一週只提供一次。"},{"w":"zealous","p":"adj.","d":"very enthusiastic and eager","c":"熱心的；狂熱的","s":"The zealous volunteers arrived early to set up the book fair, and they stayed until every box was packed.","t":"熱心的志工們提早到場佈置書展，一直留到每個箱子都打包好。"},{"w":"spur","p":"v.","d":"to encourage someone to do something","c":"激勵；鞭策","s":"Her teacher's kind words spur her to enter the writing contest, and she won second place.","t":"老師親切的話語激勵她參加寫作比賽，結果她得了第二名。"},{"w":"bestow","p":"v.","d":"to give an honour or gift to someone","c":"授予；贈予","s":"The university bestow an honorary degree on the famous writer, and she gave a moving speech to graduates.","t":"大學授予這位知名作家榮譽學位，她向畢業生發表了動人的演講。"},{"w":"benevolent","p":"adj.","d":"kind and wanting to help others","c":"仁慈的；慈善的","s":"A benevolent businessman paid for the new school bus, so children in the mountains no longer walk for hours.","t":"一位慈善的商人出資購買新校車，所以山區的孩子不必再走好幾個小時。"},{"w":"circumspect","p":"adj.","d":"careful not to take risks","c":"謹慎的","s":"Be circumspect about what you post online, because some universities sometimes check applicants' social media accounts.","t":"在網路上發文要謹慎，因為有些大學有時會查看申請者的社群媒體帳號。"},{"w":"cumbersome","p":"adj.","d":"large, heavy or complicated and difficult to use","c":"笨重的；繁瑣的","s":"The old registration system was cumbersome, so students waited in long lines for hours every semester.","t":"舊的選課系統很繁瑣，所以學生每學期都要排好幾個小時的長隊。"},{"w":"dissuade","p":"v.","d":"to persuade someone not to do something","c":"勸阻","s":"Her parents tried to dissuade her from studying drama, but she followed her dream and became an actor.","t":"她父母試圖勸阻她念戲劇，但她追隨夢想成為了演員。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (enigma – redress)","cards":[{"w":"enigma","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is mysterious and hard to understand","c":"謎；難以理解的人或事","s":"The quiet new student was an enigma to his classmates, but they discovered he was a brilliant guitarist.","t":"那位安靜的新同學對同學們來說是個謎，但他們發現他是個出色的吉他手。"},{"w":"epitomise","p":"v.","d":"to be a perfect example of something","c":"是…的典型；集中體現","s":"Our coach epitomise hard work, because she trains every morning and never misses a practice.","t":"我們的教練是努力的典範，因為她每天早上訓練，從不缺席任何一次練習。"},{"w":"exhort","p":"v.","d":"to strongly encourage someone to do something","c":"力勸；勉勵","s":"The principal exhort the graduates to keep learning, and she reminded them that education never ends.","t":"校長勉勵畢業生持續學習，並提醒他們教育永無止境。"},{"w":"extol","p":"v.","d":"to praise something very highly","c":"讚揚；頌揚","s":"Many parents extol the benefits of reading aloud, because their children learned new words quickly this way.","t":"許多家長讚揚朗讀的好處，因為他們的孩子用這種方式很快學會新單字。"},{"w":"fastidious","p":"adj.","d":"very careful about details and wanting things perfect","c":"一絲不苟的；挑剔的","s":"Our fastidious chemistry teacher checks every measurement, so our lab reports must be very accurate.","t":"我們那位一絲不苟的化學老師會檢查每一個測量值，所以我們的實驗報告必須非常精確。"},{"w":"heterogeneous","p":"adj.","d":"made up of many different kinds","c":"異質的；多樣混雜的","s":"The class is very heterogeneous, and it includes students from five countries with very different levels of English.","t":"這個班級非常多元混雜，包括來自五個國家、英文程度差異很大的學生。"},{"w":"impeccable","p":"adj.","d":"perfect, with no mistakes","c":"無可挑剔的；完美的","s":"Her English pronunciation is impeccable, so many people think she grew up in an English-speaking country.","t":"她的英文發音無可挑剔，所以很多人以為她在英語系國家長大。"},{"w":"impromptu","p":"adj.","d":"done without planning or preparation","c":"即興的；臨時的","s":"The teacher asked me to give an impromptu speech, but I felt ready because we practise speaking every week.","t":"老師要我做即興演講，但我覺得已經準備好了，因為我們每週都練習口說。"},{"w":"incisive","p":"adj.","d":"clear, sharp and showing deep understanding","c":"敏銳的；一針見血的","s":"His incisive questions impressed the professor, and she invited him to join her research team.","t":"他一針見血的提問讓教授印象深刻，她邀請他加入研究團隊。"},{"w":"innocuous","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful or offensive","c":"無害的；無惡意的","s":"The joke seemed innocuous to him, but it hurt his classmate's feelings, so he apologised the next day.","t":"這個玩笑對他來說似乎無傷大雅，但它傷了同學的心，所以他隔天道了歉。"},{"w":"insular","p":"adj.","d":"interested only in your own small group or country","c":"狹隘的；封閉的","s":"Students from insular communities may struggle abroad at first, but travel soon widens their view of the world.","t":"來自封閉社群的學生一開始在國外可能適應困難，但旅行很快就會拓展他們的世界觀。"},{"w":"intrepid","p":"adj.","d":"brave and not afraid of danger","c":"無畏的；勇敢的","s":"The intrepid students hiked to a remote village to teach English, and they stayed there for the whole summer.","t":"這群勇敢的學生徒步到偏遠村莊教英文，並在那裡待了一整個暑假。"},{"w":"nascent","p":"adj.","d":"just starting to develop","c":"新生的；初期的","s":"AI tutoring is still a nascent industry, so nobody knows how much it will change schools.","t":"人工智慧家教仍是新興的產業，所以沒有人知道它會改變學校多少。"},{"w":"obstinate","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to change your opinion","c":"固執的","s":"He was too obstinate to accept help with maths, so his grades did not improve until he finally asked.","t":"他太固執了，不肯接受數學方面的幫助，所以直到他終於開口求助，成績才進步。"},{"w":"ostracise","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to include someone in a group","c":"排擠；排斥","s":"Some children ostracise classmates who look different, so teachers must teach respect from an early age.","t":"有些孩子會排擠外表不同的同學，所以老師必須從小教導尊重。"},{"w":"paucity","p":"n.","d":"a lack of something","c":"缺乏；不足","s":"There is a paucity of English teachers in rural areas, so many students there learn through online classes.","t":"偏鄉地區英文老師不足，所以那裡許多學生透過線上課程學習。"},{"w":"penchant","p":"n.","d":"a strong liking for something","c":"嗜好；偏好","s":"She has a penchant for long words in her essays, but her teacher wants her to write more simply.","t":"她寫作文時偏好用長字，但老師希望她寫得簡單一點。"},{"w":"perfunctory","p":"adj.","d":"done quickly with little care or interest","c":"敷衍的","s":"He gave a perfunctory apology to the teacher, so she asked him to think again about what he had done.","t":"他向老師做了敷衍的道歉，所以她要他再想想自己做了什麼。"},{"w":"prowess","p":"n.","d":"great skill at doing something","c":"高超技能；本領","s":"Her prowess in mathematics was clear from an early age, and she won her first contest at nine.","t":"她在數學上的過人本領從小就很明顯，九歲就贏得了第一場比賽。"},{"w":"reprimand","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially that they did wrong","c":"斥責；訓誡","s":"The teacher reprimand the boys for running in the hallway, but she did it quietly and kindly.","t":"老師訓誡那些在走廊奔跑的男孩，但她說得很小聲也很和善。"},{"w":"reticent","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to say what you think or feel","c":"沉默寡言的；不願多說的","s":"Many students are reticent in large classes, but they speak much more in small group discussions.","t":"許多學生在大班級裡不太願意發言，但在小組討論時說得多很多。"},{"w":"rhetoric","p":"n.","d":"speech or writing meant to persuade, sometimes without real meaning","c":"修辭；空話","s":"Politicians use a lot of rhetoric about better schools, but teachers want to see real money and action.","t":"政客們發表許多關於改善學校的漂亮話，但老師想看到真正的經費和行動。"},{"w":"squander","p":"v.","d":"to waste money, time or chances","c":"浪費；揮霍","s":"Don't squander your free periods on games, because those hours can make a big difference before exams.","t":"別把空堂時間浪費在玩遊戲上，因為那些時間在考前可能帶來很大的差別。"},{"w":"wary","p":"adj.","d":"careful because you think there may be danger or problems","c":"謹慎的；提防的","s":"Parents are wary of new learning apps, because some of them collect children's personal data.","t":"家長對新的學習應用程式很提防，因為其中有些會蒐集兒童的個人資料。"},{"w":"redress","p":"v.","d":"to correct something unfair","c":"糾正；補救","s":"The government built new schools in rural areas to redress the gap, but good teachers are still hard to find.","t":"政府在鄉村地區興建新學校以弭平差距，但優秀的老師仍然難找。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"hit the books","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start studying hard","c":"開始用功讀書","s":"The final exams start next week, so I need to hit the books instead of going to the cinema tonight.","t":"期末考下週開始，所以我今晚得開始用功讀書，而不是去看電影。"},{"w":"learn by heart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to memorise something so you can say it perfectly","c":"背熟；牢記","s":"We had to learn by heart a short poem, and each student recited it in front of the class.","t":"我們必須背熟一首短詩，而且每位學生都要在全班面前背誦。"},{"w":"pass with flying colours","p":"v.phr.","d":"to pass a test very successfully","c":"以優異成績通過","s":"She was nervous about the speaking test, but she pass with flying colours and got the highest score in her class.","t":"她對口說測驗很緊張，但她以優異成績通過，拿到班上最高分。"},{"w":"teacher's pet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a student whom the teacher seems to like best","c":"老師的寵兒","s":"Some classmates call him the teacher's pet, but he simply works hard and asks good questions.","t":"有些同學叫他老師的寵兒，但他只是很努力又會問好問題。"},{"w":"brush up on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to practise and improve a skill you used to have","c":"複習；重溫","s":"I need to brush up on my Japanese before the trip, because I have forgotten many useful phrases.","t":"出發前我需要複習一下日文，因為我忘了很多實用的句子。"},{"w":"show of hands","p":"n.phr.","d":"a vote where people raise their hands","c":"舉手表決","s":"The teacher asked for a show of hands, and most students chose to go to the science museum.","t":"老師請大家舉手表決，大部分學生選擇去科學博物館。"},{"w":"trial and error","p":"n.phr.","d":"trying different ways until you find one that works","c":"反覆試驗；試誤","s":"We built the bridge model by trial and error, and it finally held two kilograms after five attempts.","t":"我們用反覆試驗的方式做橋梁模型，試了五次後它終於撐住了兩公斤。"},{"w":"jot down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to write something quickly","c":"匆匆記下","s":"Please jot down any new words during the video, and we will check their meanings together afterwards.","t":"請在看影片時記下任何生字，之後我們會一起查它們的意思。"},{"w":"look up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to search for information in a book or online","c":"查詢（字典等）","s":"When I find a new word, I look up its meaning, and then I write an example sentence in my notebook.","t":"我遇到生字時會查它的意思，然後在筆記本上寫一個例句。"},{"w":"read between the lines","p":"v.phr.","d":"to understand a hidden meaning","c":"領會言外之意","s":"The question asks you to read between the lines, because the writer never says directly how she feels.","t":"這題要你讀出言外之意，因為作者從未直接說出她的感受。"},{"w":"growth mindset","p":"n.phr.","d":"the belief that ability can grow with effort","c":"成長型思維","s":"Teachers try to build a growth mindset in students, so they see mistakes as chances to learn rather than signs of failure.","t":"老師們試著培養學生的成長型思維，讓他們把錯誤視為學習的機會，而不是失敗的象徵。"},{"w":"practice makes perfect","p":"phr.","d":"doing something often is the way to become good at it","c":"熟能生巧","s":"My piano teacher always says \"practice makes perfect\", so I play for thirty minutes every day.","t":"我的鋼琴老師總是說「熟能生巧」，所以我每天彈三十分鐘。"},{"w":"hand in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give your work to a teacher","c":"繳交","s":"Please hand in your reports by Friday, or the teacher will take ten points off your score.","t":"請在星期五前繳交報告，否則老師會扣十分。"},{"w":"keep up with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move or learn at the same speed as others","c":"跟上","s":"He missed two weeks of school, so it was hard to keep up with the rest of the class.","t":"他缺課兩週，所以很難跟上班上其他同學。"},{"w":"get the hang of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn how to do something","c":"掌握訣竅；學會","s":"Coding seemed impossible at first, but I get the hang of it after a few weeks of practice.","t":"一開始寫程式似乎不可能，但練習幾週後我就掌握了訣竅。"},{"w":"cut corners","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something badly to save time or effort","c":"偷工減料；走捷徑","s":"Don't cut corners on your science project, because the judges will check every step of your method.","t":"做科學專題別偷工減料，因為評審會檢查你方法中的每一個步驟。"},{"w":"pay attention to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to listen or watch carefully","c":"注意","s":"Please pay attention to the instructions, because the order of the steps is very important in this experiment.","t":"請注意操作說明，因為這個實驗中步驟的順序非常重要。"},{"w":"learn the hard way","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn something through a bad experience","c":"從慘痛經驗中學到","s":"I didn't back up my files, so I learn the hard way when my laptop crashed the night before the deadline.","t":"我沒有備份檔案，所以截止日前一晚筆電當機時，我從慘痛經驗中學到了教訓。"},{"w":"learn from one's mistakes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to improve by understanding what you did wrong","c":"從錯誤中學習","s":"Ken failed his first driving test, but he learn from one's mistakes and passed easily the second time.","t":"肯第一次駕照考試沒過，但他從錯誤中學習，第二次輕鬆通過了。"},{"w":"self-fulfilling prophecy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a belief that makes itself come true","c":"自我應驗的預言","s":"If teachers expect a student to fail, it can become a self-fulfilling prophecy, because the student may stop trying.","t":"如果老師預期某位學生會失敗，這可能會成為自我應驗的預言，因為學生可能會放棄努力。"}]}];
